WEBVTT

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.200
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshi Oike.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.710
Yome-san Rokakku Tako Nishiki.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:33.340
Shi Aya Bu Taka Matsu Man Gojyou.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.930
Setta Chara Chara Uonotana.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.930
Sandals, "Crack Crack", Fish rack

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.390
Rokujyou Hijyou toorisugi,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.390
Pass the sixth and seventh,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.730
Hachijyou koereba Touji michi.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.730
and if you pass the eighth, you'll be at Touji road.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.860
Kujyou Oujite Todomesasu.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.860
And the end is at the ninth.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.000
Detective Conan — Crossroad In The Ancient Capital

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.590
I'm high school detective, Kudou Shinichi.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.520
<i>Original Story: Aoyama Gosho</i>

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.430
When I went to an amusement park
with my childhood friend Mouri Ran,

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.520
I witnessed a suspicious
transaction between some men in black.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.390
<i>Script: Furuuichi Issei</i>

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.900
Because my attention was focused on the transaction,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.980
I didn't notice another member approach me from behind.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.450
<i>Music: Oono Katsuo</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.400
I was given a poison.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.280
When I came to,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.830
my body had shrunk!

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.620
<i>Vice Director: Akira Nishimori</i>

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.250
If they found out that Kudou Shinichi was still alive,

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.670
they would come after me again and
endanger the lives of those around me.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.170
<i>Character Design: Sudou Masatomo</i>

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.130
Following Professor Agasa's
advice, I decided to hide my identity.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.920
<i>Art Director: Shibuya Yukihiro</i>

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.920
<i>Construction: Nishi Kayoko</i>

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.340
When Ran asked who I was, I
blurted out "Edogawa Conan".

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.340
Books: "Edogawa Ranpo Volume 13, 14, 15" and "Conan Doyle"

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.430
<i>Director of Photography: Nomura Takashi</i>

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.430
<i>Director of Acoustics: Kobayashi Katsuyoshi</i>

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.380
In order to find more information about the men in black,

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.220
I moved in with Ran and her father, who is a detective.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.280
I'm the high school detective of Osaka,

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.610
Hattori Heiji.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.070
My strong reasoning and kendo skills,

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.490
Note: "Kendo" is the Japanese martial art practiced by samurai.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.950
were passed on to me by my father who works
in the Osaka Prefectural Police Headquarters.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.830
and my bravery was inherited from,

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:24.790
my mother.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.460
By the way, I inherited my
dark-colored skin from my grandfather.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.880
They used to say "Hattori of
the West" and "Kudou of the East",

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.090
Both of us were equally well-known, but ...

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:41.390
<i>Edogawa Conan: Takayama Minami</i>

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.260
Kudou really is something.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:43.550
With the help of Professor Agasa,
an inventor of strange machines,

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.850
<i>Mouri Kogorou: Kamiya Akira</i>

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.850
<i>Mouri Ran: Yamazaki Wakana</i>

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.850
He has solved many cases.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.350
There are people who know Kudou's real identity,

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:55.230
<i>Inspector Megure: Chafurin</i>

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:55.230
<i>Dr. Agasa: Ogata Kenichi</i>

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.310
besides Professor Agasa and myself.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.610
Kudou's father and mother,

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.610
<i>Kudou Shinichi: Yamaguchi Kappei</i>

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:59.490
and a girl who attends the same
elementary school as Kudou, Haibara Ai.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.950
This little girl used to be in the
same organization as the men in black.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.910
But in order to escape,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.370
she drank the same poison that Kudou was given,

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.620
and her body shrank as well.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.300
<i>Producers:</i>

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.300
<i>Suwa Michiko</i>

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.300
<i>Yoshioka Masahito</i>

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.170
By the way, I have a childhood
friend who's in the same grade as me.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.880
Her name is Tooyama Kazuha. She's a fussy woman.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.340
Who are you calling fussy!?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.720
Hey! Don't show up so suddenly, idiot!

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.100
You're the idiot!

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:27.810
Who were you talking to?

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:28.930
Who?

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.640
I'm making it easier to
understand for everybody that's watching!

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:32.650
Right?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:33.650
Huh?

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.020
Is something wrong with your head?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.360
You're the one who's got something wrong.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.610
Even though I've become
small, my mind is still the same.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:42.360
<i>Director: Kanetsugu Kodama</i>

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.820
There is only one truth!

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.660
Beika, Beika station, the exit will be ...

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.000
So you won't be able to come back for a while.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.380
Yeah, I'm pretty busy investigating a case right now.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:56.170
Oh.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.340
It's been cold these past few
days, so you'd better be careful.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.050
Same to you. Don't sleep with your stomach exposed.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.680
I don't sleep with my stomach exposed! Idiot!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.560
Yoshinoyama!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:13.560
Note: Yoshinoyama refers to a play written about two characters in
Japanese history, Minamoto Yoshitsune and his concubine, Shizuka Gozen.
They separated when Yoshitsune's brother pressed him to flee to northern Japan.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.020
Treading through the white snow of the mountain,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.810
longing for a trace of life to appear ...

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.610
It's as if you two were Yoshitsune and Shizuka Gozen.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.070
What!?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.530
Is there something wrong about
worrying for your childhood friend?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.070
I'm going to hang up now because my dad's being noisy.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:28.870
Ah ... Hey!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.450
Really ...

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.870
Next time I'll call when he's not around.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.250
Yoshitsune and Shizuka Gozen?

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.840
After they separated, they never reunited ...

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.550
Hey, hey.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.260
Tokyo — Nishikuni Tachi City

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.560
Kamei no Rokurou (35)

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:58.480
Note: Everyone here has numbers in their
name, "Rokurou"= 6, "Hachirou"= 8, "Shichirou"= 7

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.560
Kataoka no Hachirou (34)

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.560
Washinoo no Shichirou (35)

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.450
He's so slow, that Benkei.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.670
Yeah, he claimed he had solved the mystery.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.960
He was the most enthusiastic about this thing.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:26.930
Kataoka!

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.210
Osaka — Late at night

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.210
Neyagawashi "Takohei"

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:11.140
Note: "shi"= 4

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.470
Bizen no Heishirou (35)

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.690
Kyoto — Early dawn

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.480
East Mountain District "Snack Jirou"

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.190
Surugano Jirou (32)

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.230
Note: "ji"= 2

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.130
—Several days later—

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.130
Tokyo — Police headquarters

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.460
The results of the investigation show,

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.130
five victims in Tokyo, Osaka, and Kyoto.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:54.220
Note: Genji refers to "Genji Monogatari," which translates to "Genji Tales," written by
Murasaki Shikibu. Genji had a younger brother named "Hotaru" which means "firefly."

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.220
It was confirmed that they're
members of the robbery group, Genjibotaru.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:53.850
Therefore,

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.260
this case ...

00:06:54.760 --> 00:07:00.190
Kyoto Prefectural Police

00:06:54.760 --> 00:07:00.190
Ayanokouji Fumimaru

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.060
Satou-san,

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.520
Inspector Ayanokouji of the Kyoto Prefectural Police,

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.650
was in the same class as Inspector Shiratori?

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:02.310
Yes.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.270
He's of noble descent and is called "The Royal Inspector".

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.820
Look, in his left pocket.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:08.400
Eh?

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.030
What is that?

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.820
His pet chipmunk.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.120
He takes it everywhere.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.870
He's even weirder than Shiratori.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.170
Genjibotaru has been stealing famous Buddhist statues.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.710
Their activities have been centered in,

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:27.500
Tokyo, Osaka, and Kyoto since 1991.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.050
Their major trait is,

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.720
their members are named after servants of Yoshitsune,

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:36.560
and hold identical Yoshitsune Chronicles.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.510
Yoshitsune Chronicles

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.680
Their leader is Yoshitsune.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Yoshitsune

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Benkei

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Suruga no Jirou

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Ise no Saburou

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Bizen no Heishirou

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Kamei no Rokurou

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Washinoo
no Shichirou

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:47.190
Kataoka
no Hachirou

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:40.730
Following are:

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:41.600
Benkei,

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.810
Ise no Saburou,

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:43.940
all totaling to eight members.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.360
This time, all but three have been killed,

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.400
and their Yoshitsune Chronicles have been stolen.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.570
Any leads on the suspect?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.660
Osaka Prefectural Police

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.660
Inspector Ootaki

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.820
All we know is that the suspect is
skilled in swordmanship and archery.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.500
As to Yoshitsune, Benkei, and Ise no Saburou,

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.920
we do not know their ages or genders.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.250
At any rate,

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:10.050
the culprit and the remaining
members of the group must be arrested.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.760
We will do our best to continue the investigation.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.260
Hattori Residence

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:24.270
Magazine: "Yoshitsune of the 20th Century, The Head of a Robbery Group"

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.100
Yoshitsune of the 20th century,

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.940
The head of a robbery group.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:50.800
Heiji! Are you there?

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.350
That's not good. This is important to you, right?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.350
Uh, y-yeah, I should put it away.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:06.600
Heiji, are you going out?

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.570
Yeah, there's something I wanted to check out.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.190
Was there something you wanted?

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:14.110
No.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.610
I just thought you'd like to see
the Sakura blossoms at Tomorogi.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:18.990
But, that's alright.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:19.870
Really?

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.790
Then I'll be leaving.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.660
Take care!

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:25.460
Yes.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.210
Why do I have to see him off with a smiling face!?

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:41.350
As I thought, Kyoto is the
hometown of all Japanese people!

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.430
Alright, I brought you here on a special occasion,

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.350
so don't get in my way.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.640
Yes sir.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.860
Conan-kun's so lucky, he went to Kyoto.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:56.360
There was a request for Mouri
from a temple called Sannou Temple.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.280
We want to go to Kyoto, too!

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:01.070
Hmm ...

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.950
I could take you there, but ...

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.160
Really?

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.000
I can meet Conan-kun!

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.830
Kyoto! Kyoto!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:10.710
Tomorrow is ...

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.420
However, that's if you can answer this quiz.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:14.670
Here we go.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.130
You probably aren't going to take us, right?

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:18.340
Isn't this alright?

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.010
Hear him out.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.890
It'll kill some time.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:24.850
Hey, what should we do?

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.480
Let's try.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.190
Alright.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.900
The three of you know who Benkei is, right?

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:32.560
Yes.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.610
He's Yoshitsune's servant.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:35.690
Hey,

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.360
Who's Yoshitsune?

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.400
His childhood name is Ushiwakamaru.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.490
And on Kyoto's Gojyouoohashi,

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.370
he defeated Benkei, who was
aiming to get his 1000th sword.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.500
Benkei then became his servant.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.330
That is Minamoto Yoshitsune.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:49.710
At that time,

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.830
The Genji clan and Heike clan were fighting,

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.380
and Yoshitsune defeated the Heike clan.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.760
But he was hated by his older brother, Yoritomo.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:02.050
Iwate prefecture

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.300
He committed suicide,

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.140
at Koromogawa of Hiraizumi,
where today's Iwate prefecture would be.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.810
Wow, you seem to know a lot about him.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.310
Now the question is:

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.480
Benkei had a first love named Uzune.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.860
When he found out that she
was going to marry another man,

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.940
Benkei ...

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:17.730
1. Became Angry

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.650
2. Became Happy

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.070
3. Cried

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:22.950
So, which one is it?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.780
His first love!?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.330
Of course he will be angry!

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.630
There's no reason for him to be happy!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.800
So you say the answer is "Became Angry"?

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.010
He cried.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.010
The answer is "Cried".

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.810
You got the idea from "Benkei's crying spot", right?

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.480
I'm no match for you, Ai-kun.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:53.770
"Benkei's crying spot"?

00:11:54.440 --> 00:12:00.280
Even a guy as strong as Benkei has a
spot that hurts enough to cry if kicked.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.360
That's right here. "Mukouzune" is "Benkei's crying spot".

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.070
But ...

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.490
What does that have to do with the quiz?

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.200
Uh,

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.790
Well that is ...

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:12.910
I get it!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.340
The people getting married are "Muko" and "Uzune".

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.340
Note: "Muko" translates to groom.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.130
Muko and Uzune make "Mukouzune".

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:23.550
It's another big pun.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:27.760
But since we got the right
answer, we can go to Kyoto now!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:31.140
Uh ... No, because Ai got the right answer ...

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:35.310
Haibara-san is part of the Detective Boys, too!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.690
Don't leave Haibara-san out!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:43.320
My mom told me not to become
an adult that goes back on his word.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.000
Thank you very much.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:59.630
Thanks.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.590
Sannou Temple

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.850
Even if you say so, this doesn't leave here.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.100
Ryuen (34)

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.100
Monk of Sannou Temple

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:13.980
Oh, Mouri-san!

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.600
Thank you for coming to such a far away place.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.820
I am Ryuen, the one who called you.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:22.570
Please allow me to introduce you to,

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.450
Enkai (65)

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.450
Chief Priest of Sannou Temple

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.650
The Chief Priest, Enkai.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.820
these three are supporters of this temple.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.620
Sakura Shouzou (51)

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.620
Antique Arts Dealer

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:30.870
Sakura Shouzou-san.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.910
He manages an antique art
dealership on Teramachi Road.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.670
You're the famous detective Mouri Kogorou?

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.840
Ah, really? Am I that famous?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:47.090
Mizuo Shuntarou (33)

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:47.090
Noh Performer

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.170
Next to him is,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:47.340
Note: Noh theater is a special theatrical performance over 600
years old. It incorporates the Noh masks and a lot of dancing.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.220
The young master of the Mizuo style Noh theater,

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:46.760
Mizuo Shuntarou.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.430
And this is Saijou Taiga-san,
the owner of a used book store.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:52.350
Saijou Taiga (35)

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:52.350
Used Book Store Owner

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:52.600
Nice to meet you.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:56.270
Well, they're all more of friends in kendo than supporters.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.850
Oh, everyone is skilled in kendo?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.980
No wonder you are so vigorous at an old age.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:03.860
Huh ...

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.070
Kendo friends?

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:06.650
By the way,

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:12.030
There is a wooden Buddha
unveiled every 12 years at this temple.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:12.740
Yes.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.290
The main statue of this temple, the Healing Buddha.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.000
It will be presented for worship two days after tomorrow.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.210
We are looking forward to it.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.590
Well,

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.800
I believe the Healing Buddha will be delighted.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.720
What are you saying!?

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.850
The principal object of worship was stolen!?

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:33.470
Yes.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.720
It has been eight years since it happened.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.980
Sunlight bodhisattva

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.060
On the right, as one faces it, is the Sunlight bodhisattva.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.980
Moonlight bodhisattva

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.030
On the left, as one faces it, is the Moonlight bodhisattva.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:49.110
The Healing Buddha in the
center was subject to burglary.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:52.910
I was going to report it to the police immediately,

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.740
but the chief priest stopped me.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:15:00.830
He said that there may be a
chance that it would return one day.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.670
How easygoing of him.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:04.590
And,

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.460
Eight years from the event,

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.510
five days ago,

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.590
in the temple's mailbox was this.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:11.890
Sannou Temple

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:12.840
No stamps,

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:15.560
and no sender.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.810
Solve the puzzle in the picture,

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:23.400
and you will find the whereabouts of the Buddhist statue.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.570
What is this picture?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.660
Thanks, sir.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.870
As I thought, there aren't that many witnesses,

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.200
to a crime committed in early dawn.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.960
Thief!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.040
Out of the way!

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:50.880
That hurts!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.800
That was "Benkei's crying spot".

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.300
It hurts a lot, that spot.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:15:59.020
Here.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.180
It's yours, right?

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:01.560
Thank you.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.940
That was very kind of you.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.730
Well, not at all.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:10.570
Yamakura Tae (52)

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:10.570
Mistress of a Tea House
in Miyagawachou

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.480
I manage a tea house in Miyagawachou.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.030
My name is Yamakura Tae.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.660
Take yours out as well.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.030
Chika Suzu (19)

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.030
Dancer

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:15.320
Yes.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:17.450
I am Chika Suzu.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.620
Nice to meet you.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.000
How should we thank you?

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.840
I didn't do very much, so it's alright.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.010
Then please come visit next time.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.300
Take care going home.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:34.800
Thank you.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.230
What is this picture?

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.780
On the very top row, the fifth row,

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.410
a cicada, Tengu, and goldfish is drawn.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:57.620
Note: Tengu is a long-nosed demon that often appears in Japanese literature.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.570
And below that, on the fourth row,

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.080
are a chicken and a ...

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.620
Loach?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.040
The yellow loach looks disgusting.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.330
What's this dot-like mark?

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:07.710
It's probably just a stain.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.710
Between the second and third rows,

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:13.510
there's a violet, Tengu, and Mt. Fuji.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.880
Beside them is an acorn.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.010
Father,

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.600
will we be able to find it
before the two days after tomorrow?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.680
D-Don't worry,

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.440
if it's up to me, this is not a mystery at all.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.650
Hey hey, is that really true?

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.900
Let's leave the searching for
the Buddhist statue up to the pros,

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.610
and go sightseeing in Kyoto.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.320
Ah, go right ahead.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.570
If you guys are here, you'll only be disturbing me.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:41.830
Actually, I contacted Kazuha,

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.620
and she's going to be guiding us around Kyoto tomorrow.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:48.370
Hattori-kun has some other plans, so he won't be coming.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.460
A guy whose girlfriend is already
decided doesn't need to be there.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:52.960
Oh ...

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:54.550
That guy isn't coming.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.220
Conan-kun you're coming with us, right?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.260
Uh, I'm alright.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.060
I already promised to go fishing
in the river with the kids nearby.

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:03.850
Wow,

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.310
You made friends already?

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.020
Then be careful, alright?

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.190
Uh, yeah.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:11.730
The one who stole the
Buddhist statue from Sannou Temple,

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.940
must be the Genjibotaru group.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:15.610
However,

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.910
who sent this picture and with what intentions?

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.490
Also, what's the connection between the five murders?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.040
Genjibotaru ...

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.790
Speaking of Yoshitsune and Benkei,

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.130
that must be the place.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.010
Gojyou Bridge

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.980
There seems to be nothing here
related to this mysterious picture.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.860
On the Gojyou bridge of Kyoto,

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.780
the large man Benkei,

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.070
raised his long halberd.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:18:59.950
Aiming at Ushiwakamaru, he slashed downward.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.950
Ha-Hattori!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:11.170
The gods have done some
tasteful things for me to meet you here.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.960
Nii-chan, can you give me back my shinai?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:21.340
Note: A "shinai" is a wooden practice sword used in kendo.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.210
Oh, sorry, sorry!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.090
Thanks.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:19.590
Let's go.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.510
Make sure you practice hard!

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:27.100
Don't borrow some kid's shinai.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:28.430
Anyways,

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:30.350
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.810
Same to you, what are you doing?

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.860
As a matter of fact, the murdered
owner of the takoyaki shop in Osaka,

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:39.740
Note: "Takoyaki" are dumplings with octopus in the middle.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:39.360
was an acquaintance of mine.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.110
He was supposedly a member of a robbery group.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:46.080
I went to his shop often while I was in middle school.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.120
I'm indebted to him in a way.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.210
So, I want to find the culprit and avenge his death.

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.420
That's why you came to Kyoto.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.130
You're looking for leads to the culprit.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.590
If that's so, then I have something good to show you.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.140
I see.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.680
If you solve the mystery behind the puzzle,

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.310
not only do you find the Buddhist statue,

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.940
but it might also lead to clues about the murders.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:13.980
That's why you ...

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.770
If the Genjibotaru group was the
one who stole the Buddhist statue,

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.650
then if we go around the locations
related to Yoshitsune and Benkei,

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.320
There might be some leads
as to how to solve the mystery.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.910
I don't understand Kyoto at all.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.120
Then from now on, leave it to me.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:31.040
I'll guide you.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:38.750
Gojyouten Shrine

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:38.960
Here is Gojyouten Shrine.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:42.420
According to the Yoshitsune
Chronicles, it wasn't the Gojyou Bridge,

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.510
where they met, but here.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:46.680
How about it ...

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.220
Do you see any common features between them?

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.720
Hmm, no.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.390
There doesn't seem to be any.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.190
Then let's get going to the next spot.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.600
Something doesn't please me ...

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:01.730
Why didn't the monk from
Sannou Temple request for me?

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.360
If he were looking for a
Kansai detective, that would be me.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:06.110
Note: Kansai is the southwestern half of Japan, including Osaka.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.280
Oh, well ...

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.120
Probably because they didn't want
the police knowing about the incident.

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:12.370
You know, your dad is a
superior in the police department.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:15.580
Hmm, oh well.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:17.750
Wait a second.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.340
Now that you mention it ...

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.470
Here we are. It's right here.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.260
Benkei Stone

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.850
Benkei Stone?

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:34.600
It's said Benkei was always sitting on it,

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:36.560
or that he had thrown it from Mt. Hie.

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:38.900
There's various traditions handed down.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.190
This place doesn't have any connections either.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:43.230
Okay.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:44.740
Onwards to the next place.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:46.200
Where's the next place?

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:48.570
Keage Incline.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.950
I am Inspector Ayanokouji of
the Kyoto Prefectural Police.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:56.830
You seem to be doing some various
investigations on the Genjibotaru group.

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.330
This is different than Osaka.

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.380
Amateurs should not stick their
noses in other people's business.

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:10.350
It's a chipmunk.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:12.510
Alright?

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:19.770
There seem to be uncommon inspectors everywhere.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:23.020
Kiyomizudera Temple

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:24.730
I'm going to take a picture.

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:26.570
Let's take it in front of the Sakura blossoms.

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:27.990
It's so beautiful.

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:31.410
To be able to see such a wonderful sight ...

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:35.450
With Makoto-san would make me so happy!

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:37.580
Ran!

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:39.920
I'm just doing what you always do to me.

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:48.130
Kazuha-chan,

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:50.220
Did you get in a fight with Hattori-kun?

00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:52.850
Actually, Heiji,

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.520
came to Kyoto to investigate a case.

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:57.640
Also in Kyoto,

00:22:57.980 --> 00:22:59.810
Is Heiji's first love!

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:07.320
Keage Incline "Canal Park"

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:10.660
Yoshitsune, Perfected Great Sun Buddha

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:14.620
This one's a miss, too?

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:17.040
Why don't we have lunch?

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:18.120
Sure.

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:28.630
Sakura ...

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:33.760
When I see Sakura blossoms,
I always recall what happened,

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:35.600
Eight years ago.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.020
I was on an expedition in Kyoto's temples,

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:42.100
and when I jumped on to the temple's latticed window,

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:45.230
the grid broke.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:48.440
Then I hit my head on the floor,

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:50.110
and I lost consciousness.

00:23:51.820 --> 00:23:54.410
I don't know how long I was sleeping.

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:56.370
But when I woke up ...

00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:01.080
... koereba Touji michi.

00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:01.080
And if you pass the eighth, you'll be at Touji road.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:06.250
Kujyou Oujite Todomesasu.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:06.250
And the end is at the ninth.

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:11.260
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshi Oike

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:16.600
Yome San Rokakku Tako Nishiki

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:22.140
Shi Aya Bu Taka Matsu Man Gojyou

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:26.730
Setta Chara Chara Uonotana

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:26.730
Sandals, "Crack Crack", fish rack

00:24:56.090 --> 00:24:58.470
It was like a dream, but it's a true story.

00:25:01.430 --> 00:25:03.980
Maybe one day we'll be able to meet again.

00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:08.610
Hey.

00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:10.110
What are you laughing at?

00:25:11.780 --> 00:25:13.400
Sorry, please continue.

00:25:13.900 --> 00:25:16.570
When I come to Kyoto, I always take this with me.

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:19.870
It's a crystal ball.

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:22.830
I've seen this shape somewhere before.

00:25:23.450 --> 00:25:23.870
Really!?

00:25:24.620 --> 00:25:26.080
Does someone have the same thing?

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:27.920
No.

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:29.590
So,

00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:31.630
Does she know about this?

00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:32.920
She?

00:25:33.800 --> 00:25:35.300
Oh, you mean Kazuha?

00:25:36.260 --> 00:25:38.970
I haven't told her anything in
detail, but she seems to know about it.

00:25:39.850 --> 00:25:42.430
To begin with, she found out about it ...

00:25:43.640 --> 00:25:45.230
In a magazine interview article?

00:25:45.980 --> 00:25:46.350
Right.

00:25:47.020 --> 00:25:49.610
In Kansai's really popular information magazine,

00:25:50.360 --> 00:25:53.440
Heiji was asked about his first love.

00:25:54.150 --> 00:25:55.900
He answered that it was a girl,

00:25:56.110 --> 00:25:58.410
a little older than him that he met in third grade.

00:25:59.700 --> 00:26:02.990
Moreover, he said that there's an
important artifact that concerns this girl.

00:26:03.540 --> 00:26:06.040
They took a picture like this.

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:08.170
What is this?

00:26:08.830 --> 00:26:10.040
An ordinary crystal ball.

00:26:10.590 --> 00:26:12.250
He probably received it from that girl.

00:26:12.920 --> 00:26:14.800
Then Kazuha-chan, about that girl ...

00:26:15.210 --> 00:26:16.510
Know her? Of course not!

00:26:17.720 --> 00:26:19.890
Heiji seems to have only met her that one time.

00:26:20.470 --> 00:26:23.060
Whenever he comes to Kyoto, he looks for her.

00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:26.230
Ah, so that's why he has the crystal ball in the picture.

00:26:26.850 --> 00:26:29.940
Maybe he thinks that girl will read this article,

00:26:29.940 --> 00:26:32.230
and might contact him.

00:26:33.190 --> 00:26:34.690
See, isn't that unpleasant!?

00:26:36.240 --> 00:26:39.200
As a bonus, there's even a
picture of him taken around that time.

00:26:39.110 --> 00:26:41.620
Note: The bold letters underneath Heiji's kid picture read "Heiji in third grade"

00:26:40.910 --> 00:26:41.700
How cute!

00:26:42.070 --> 00:26:42.990
Don't you agree?

00:26:43.240 --> 00:26:44.870
Heiji was so cute back then.

00:26:46.450 --> 00:26:46.950
Ran-chan ...

00:26:47.370 --> 00:26:48.960
That isn't the problem.

00:26:49.670 --> 00:26:51.790
I don't think you should be concerned about it.

00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:54.840
Even if Hattori-kun had a first love,

00:26:55.250 --> 00:26:56.670
she's in the past.

00:26:57.630 --> 00:27:00.090
Right now, it looks like it's going well with you.

00:27:00.680 --> 00:27:01.510
However,

00:27:01.550 --> 00:27:05.390
to men, their first love is special.

00:27:06.560 --> 00:27:07.180
Sonoko!

00:27:08.770 --> 00:27:11.230
Let's stop this boring conversation.

00:27:11.650 --> 00:27:13.110
Anyway, why don't we eat some zenzai?

00:27:11.650 --> 00:27:14.270
Note: Zenzai is a dessert of sweet beans, kind of like jam.

00:27:13.810 --> 00:27:17.490
Ma'am! Three zenzai, please! And hurry!

00:27:30.500 --> 00:27:32.540
That is the west gate of Kurama Temple.

00:27:33.210 --> 00:27:35.590
Usually we'd go in from the Nioumon,

00:27:33.210 --> 00:27:36.710
Note: "Nioumon" is the "second large gate"

00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:37.880
but this way is better because it's a shortcut.

00:27:40.720 --> 00:27:43.010
Kurama Temple — Inner Sanctuary 588 meters

00:28:08.370 --> 00:28:11.290
Immobile Hall of Soujyougatani

00:28:08.830 --> 00:28:11.040
This is the Immobile Hall of Soujyougatani.

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:15.710
Ushiwakamaru met the Tengu
and was instructed in the art of war.

00:28:18.420 --> 00:28:22.010
This is definitely a good place to train in swordsmanship.

00:28:24.140 --> 00:28:27.510
Nevertheless, this tree is really big.

00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:34.060
Hattori, this place is also not ...

00:28:35.770 --> 00:28:36.480
Get down!

00:28:42.070 --> 00:28:42.820
Wait!

00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:44.200
Hey, Kudou!

00:28:59.670 --> 00:29:01.300
That guy is like Ushiwakamaru!

00:29:10.720 --> 00:29:11.270
Damn it.

00:29:13.020 --> 00:29:14.440
Here Kudou, we're going!

00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:34.500
We got him!

00:30:04.650 --> 00:30:05.740
What is he doing!?

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:21.290
Kurama Temple

00:30:29.590 --> 00:30:31.850
Kurama Temple Station

00:30:32.350 --> 00:30:34.430
Those taking the train, please hurry,

00:30:34.680 --> 00:30:35.850
the train will be leaving short ...

00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:40.270
Well, you don't have to hurry to that extent.

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:48.070
Hey, these are the train tracks.

00:30:48.400 --> 00:30:50.240
You're distracting, don't talk to me!

00:30:51.370 --> 00:30:52.700
Violation of traffic laws.

00:30:52.990 --> 00:30:54.370
You'll get your license suspended at this rate.

00:31:06.800 --> 00:31:07.630
What's his plan?

00:31:21.980 --> 00:31:22.900
Damn!

00:31:23.860 --> 00:31:25.230
We were so close ...

00:31:26.190 --> 00:31:26.820
As I thought,

00:31:27.190 --> 00:31:27.820
That was the culprit,

00:31:28.320 --> 00:31:30.950
who murdered the members of the Genjibotaru group.

00:31:31.570 --> 00:31:32.240
That's likely.

00:31:32.950 --> 00:31:35.240
However, I don't understand why he targeted you.

00:31:44.250 --> 00:31:45.130
Hattori-kun?

00:31:45.340 --> 00:31:46.380
Why are you here?

00:31:47.460 --> 00:31:47.840
Well,

00:31:48.050 --> 00:31:49.340
By chance I ran into Kud—

00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:50.130
No, this kid.

00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:51.430
And I thought we should solve,

00:31:51.970 --> 00:31:53.840
the mystery behind the picture together.

00:31:54.350 --> 00:31:54.930
And ...

00:31:55.470 --> 00:31:57.140
Were you able to solve the mystery behind the picture?

00:31:57.470 --> 00:31:57.970
Not yet.

00:31:58.720 --> 00:31:59.890
It's pretty difficult.

00:32:00.850 --> 00:32:02.900
By the way, was uncle able to solve it?

00:32:03.850 --> 00:32:05.190
Well ...

00:32:12.740 --> 00:32:15.700
Bantochou

00:32:16.740 --> 00:32:19.700
"Sakura" Tea House

00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:30.710
Note: Geisha are professional hostesses who
entertain guests through various performing arts in tea houses.

00:32:26.790 --> 00:32:29.710
Ichi Kayo

00:32:26.790 --> 00:32:29.710
Geisha

00:32:48.480 --> 00:32:52.440
Note: Maiko are apprentice geisha. It usually takes about
five years of training for them to "graduate" to full geisha status.

00:32:48.520 --> 00:32:51.440
Chika Suzu (19)

00:32:48.520 --> 00:32:51.440
Maiko

00:32:57.990 --> 00:33:00.950
Chika Suzu-chan, you're Japan's number one!

00:33:01.540 --> 00:33:03.540
Thank you, I hope it has pleased you.

00:33:04.620 --> 00:33:05.120
Come now,

00:33:05.620 --> 00:33:07.040
And serve Mouri-sensei.

00:33:07.330 --> 00:33:07.750
Yes.

00:33:19.600 --> 00:33:20.600
Pardon me.

00:33:24.390 --> 00:33:26.900
Kogorou-chan may climb to the heavens!

00:33:26.980 --> 00:33:28.650
Why don't you keep climbing!?

00:33:30.400 --> 00:33:32.400
You guys, why are you...

00:33:34.190 --> 00:33:36.200
The chief priest told us.

00:33:36.450 --> 00:33:37.410
Is that so,

00:33:37.610 --> 00:33:38.660
The chief priest...

00:33:39.410 --> 00:33:41.540
Then how about it? Would you like to join us?

00:33:41.870 --> 00:33:44.540
Excuse us for interrupting.

00:33:50.630 --> 00:33:51.000
Hey,

00:33:51.670 --> 00:33:52.920
Aren't you from Miyagawachou?

00:33:53.260 --> 00:33:53.630
Yes.

00:33:54.550 --> 00:33:55.590
I'm Chika Suzu.

00:33:56.130 --> 00:33:57.680
Thank you for the help earlier.

00:33:58.890 --> 00:34:00.220
Do you know her?

00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:01.890
Yeah, just a little bit.

00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:05.430
If I let you out of my sight for just one second ...

00:34:06.020 --> 00:34:06.640
Ran-san ...

00:34:07.100 --> 00:34:09.230
Please don't scold your father.

00:34:09.650 --> 00:34:11.820
We're the ones who invited him.

00:34:12.110 --> 00:34:12.820
That's right,

00:34:13.230 --> 00:34:15.400
we thought we could ask the famous detective,

00:34:15.690 --> 00:34:17.200
to reason the Genjibotaru case.

00:34:17.700 --> 00:34:20.660
Sakura Tea House — Mistress

00:34:18.030 --> 00:34:19.450
Talking about the Genjibotaru,

00:34:19.820 --> 00:34:23.080
don't all the members have a
copy of the Yoshitsune Chronicles?

00:34:23.450 --> 00:34:24.750
I have one too.

00:34:25.250 --> 00:34:26.870
It's a really great book.

00:34:27.410 --> 00:34:28.290
Right, used book seller?

00:34:28.580 --> 00:34:29.250
Yes.

00:34:30.130 --> 00:34:32.590
But I don't like it very much.

00:34:33.210 --> 00:34:36.420
Even if they say it's the Yoshitsune
Chronicles, it actually depicts Benkei's activities.

00:34:36.510 --> 00:34:37.840
It is the Benkei Chronicles.

00:34:38.300 --> 00:34:39.550
I like it.

00:34:40.220 --> 00:34:41.640
Especially the "Ataka no Benkei",

00:34:41.760 --> 00:34:42.430
it's the best.

00:34:42.850 --> 00:34:44.560
Ataka? What is that?

00:34:45.060 --> 00:34:46.770
It's one of the programs of the Noh theater.

00:34:47.270 --> 00:34:49.350
While escaping from Yoritomo's pursuing party,

00:34:49.810 --> 00:34:51.190
Yoshitsune and his servants,

00:34:51.480 --> 00:34:52.860
disguise themselves as mountain priests.

00:34:53.190 --> 00:34:55.480
They try to get through the Ataka checkpoint, but,

00:34:55.900 --> 00:34:59.070
Yoshitsune's disguise is almost seen through.

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:01.910
Benkei used his Kongoubou,

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:03.910
Note: Kongoubou is a special staff that mountain priests carry.

00:35:02.200 --> 00:35:03.620
to hit Yoshitsune at once.

00:35:04.870 --> 00:35:05.540
Why?

00:35:06.500 --> 00:35:08.580
In order to deceive the checkpoint guards.

00:35:09.210 --> 00:35:13.420
No one would ever believe that a
servant would hit his master with a staff.

00:35:13.960 --> 00:35:14.500
Then,

00:35:14.750 --> 00:35:17.710
Yoshitsune and his party were able
to safely pass through the checkpoint.

00:35:18.470 --> 00:35:21.800
Later, when Benkei apologized with tears,

00:35:22.430 --> 00:35:25.390
Yoshitsune praised him for his quick wits.

00:35:26.180 --> 00:35:27.980
You can understand how deep their bond was.

00:35:28.390 --> 00:35:29.520
It's a good story.

00:35:32.230 --> 00:35:35.520
I'm sorry, but I haven't had much sleep lately.

00:35:35.900 --> 00:35:39.240
May I rest in one of the rooms downstairs?

00:35:39.400 --> 00:35:40.200
If that's the case,

00:35:40.530 --> 00:35:44.160
there are no other guests
tonight, so take the room next to...

00:35:44.370 --> 00:35:47.160
No thank you, I can settle down better downstairs.

00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:48.910
Do you think,

00:35:49.660 --> 00:35:51.080
you can wake me up at nine?

00:35:53.080 --> 00:35:55.590
Please enjoy yourselves everybody.

00:36:02.550 --> 00:36:04.470
Wow! You can see the river!

00:36:04.970 --> 00:36:06.100
That is the Kamogawa.

00:36:04.970 --> 00:36:08.100
Note: "Gawa" is suffix for river.

00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:08.270
The Sakura blossoms are beautiful.

00:36:08.350 --> 00:36:09.730
Yes, they really are.

00:36:10.480 --> 00:36:11.980
Ran, come and see.

00:36:12.940 --> 00:36:16.440
It's good to see the Sakura blossoms
from the river bed of Kamogawa as a couple.

00:36:17.020 --> 00:36:21.740
However, the view from the river
that flows beneath this building,

00:36:22.070 --> 00:36:23.570
Misogigawa, is exceptional.

00:36:24.280 --> 00:36:25.620
It really is beautiful.

00:36:25.700 --> 00:36:27.780
Yeah, it's beautiful.

00:36:28.200 --> 00:36:30.500
Your fingers are like a white fish.

00:36:30.790 --> 00:36:32.040
I almost want to eat it!

00:36:35.710 --> 00:36:37.210
Did you get injured?

00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:38.920
Yes, a little bit.

00:36:39.670 --> 00:36:41.630
Let Kogorou heal it for you.

00:36:42.050 --> 00:36:43.300
Stop it and act properly!

00:36:44.300 --> 00:36:45.010
Haha.

00:36:45.220 --> 00:36:46.600
This guy will never learn.

00:36:47.010 --> 00:36:47.470
Hey,

00:36:48.100 --> 00:36:48.810
Look at that!

00:36:51.520 --> 00:36:52.680
Inspector Ayanokouji!

00:36:53.230 --> 00:36:55.020
What is he doing at a place like that?

00:36:55.850 --> 00:36:56.400
You guys,

00:36:56.690 --> 00:36:59.520
should see the evening cherry
blossoms from the balcony below.

00:37:00.280 --> 00:37:02.240
Tonight the clouds will clear up,

00:37:02.530 --> 00:37:03.900
and a good moon will come out.

00:37:04.610 --> 00:37:05.280
Let's go.

00:37:05.530 --> 00:37:05.990
Yes.

00:37:06.240 --> 00:37:06.910
It sounds great.

00:37:07.370 --> 00:37:08.830
I'm going to stay here.

00:37:09.280 --> 00:37:09.830
Me too.

00:37:10.290 --> 00:37:10.950
Why?

00:37:11.750 --> 00:37:13.370
Are you anxious about that dancing girl?

00:37:13.830 --> 00:37:14.500
Idiot ...

00:37:14.960 --> 00:37:16.120
Don't ask anything pointless.

00:37:28.390 --> 00:37:29.100
Damn!

00:37:29.640 --> 00:37:31.640
That guy's engine is full throttle!

00:37:32.140 --> 00:37:33.730
He's constantly like that.

00:37:34.230 --> 00:37:37.060
Chika Suzu-chan, revenge, revenge.

00:37:37.400 --> 00:37:38.360
I'm going to the bathroom as well.

00:37:39.310 --> 00:37:41.230
It's alright, I'm not drunk yet.

00:37:41.900 --> 00:37:42.820
You stay with Mouri-sensei.

00:37:43.240 --> 00:37:43.570
Yes.

00:37:44.490 --> 00:37:45.900
Alright, here I go!

00:37:47.530 --> 00:37:47.910
Oh,

00:37:48.450 --> 00:37:49.530
The moon is coming out.

00:37:54.870 --> 00:37:55.540
The moon.

00:37:57.170 --> 00:37:57.580
What's wrong?

00:37:58.170 --> 00:37:58.670
No,

00:37:59.330 --> 00:38:02.380
It just reminded me of when I was
supposed to meet Ran somewhere.

00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:05.340
When I remembered our arranged meeting,

00:38:05.760 --> 00:38:07.220
it was already two hours past the set time.

00:38:07.630 --> 00:38:08.680
That's pretty bad.

00:38:09.640 --> 00:38:12.510
I thought that she wouldn't be waiting anymore.

00:38:13.270 --> 00:38:15.560
But for the time being, I went to our meeting place.

00:38:26.740 --> 00:38:27.280
Who is it?

00:38:33.910 --> 00:38:34.580
I'm sorry Ran.

00:38:35.370 --> 00:38:36.120
Actually I ...

00:38:36.410 --> 00:38:37.040
Completely ...

00:38:37.460 --> 00:38:38.460
I'm so glad,

00:38:39.120 --> 00:38:42.380
I thought that something had
happened to you, and I was really worried.

00:38:48.970 --> 00:38:50.300
It was then, huh?

00:38:50.590 --> 00:38:54.350
When your thoughts changed
about her being just a childhood friend.

00:38:55.100 --> 00:38:55.890
Idiot!

00:38:56.390 --> 00:38:57.310
It's not like that.

00:38:59.440 --> 00:39:01.310
Since a long time ago, I've been ...

00:39:03.820 --> 00:39:04.610
Even now,

00:39:05.280 --> 00:39:06.860
she's still waiting for me.

00:39:11.240 --> 00:39:12.370
What's the matter, Ran-chan?

00:39:14.160 --> 00:39:14.790
Nothing.

00:39:17.870 --> 00:39:19.080
That guy, Heiji,

00:39:19.500 --> 00:39:20.670
he really makes me angry.

00:39:21.040 --> 00:39:21.420
But ...

00:39:22.380 --> 00:39:23.840
Kazuha-chan, I envy you.

00:39:24.170 --> 00:39:24.500
Eh?

00:39:24.960 --> 00:39:25.460
Because,

00:39:26.420 --> 00:39:28.220
you can meet him whenever you want to.

00:39:30.130 --> 00:39:30.970
Ran-chan.

00:39:31.970 --> 00:39:33.010
That's true.

00:39:33.510 --> 00:39:36.060
I can't easily meet with Makoto-san either.

00:39:36.930 --> 00:39:39.100
A maiden's worries are endless.

00:39:39.600 --> 00:39:40.390
Here we go!

00:39:40.440 --> 00:39:41.650
Compared to us,

00:39:42.310 --> 00:39:44.560
those old guys are energetic.

00:39:45.650 --> 00:39:48.990
Tiger, tiger, tiger, tiger.

00:40:12.260 --> 00:40:12.970
Sakura-han,

00:40:13.470 --> 00:40:14.590
it's nine.

00:40:15.050 --> 00:40:15.640
Sakura-han?

00:40:16.890 --> 00:40:17.760
Pardon me.

00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:18.890
Oh?

00:40:20.100 --> 00:40:21.100
Where did he go?

00:40:25.770 --> 00:40:26.820
Surely not ...

00:40:36.450 --> 00:40:37.280
Sakura-han?

00:40:42.370 --> 00:40:42.710
Oh?

00:40:49.710 --> 00:40:51.260
What? Who screamed?

00:40:51.880 --> 00:40:53.050
Someone!

00:40:55.510 --> 00:40:56.340
What's the matter?

00:40:57.300 --> 00:40:58.560
Sa-Sakura-han is ...

00:41:03.190 --> 00:41:04.900
Sa-Sakura-han ...

00:41:05.480 --> 00:41:07.190
No one can go inside.

00:41:07.480 --> 00:41:07.860
Ran,

00:41:08.190 --> 00:41:09.320
call the police!

00:41:09.730 --> 00:41:10.150
Yes.

00:41:12.030 --> 00:41:14.990
A sharp edged tool cut his carotid artery.

00:41:15.530 --> 00:41:16.780
It's a magnificent slit.

00:41:17.320 --> 00:41:19.700
This could have been done by the
same criminal from the series of cases.

00:41:20.450 --> 00:41:20.990
You.

00:41:21.160 --> 00:41:23.120
I thought I'd seen you from somewhere.

00:41:23.500 --> 00:41:25.830
Are you the high school detective, Hattori Heiji?

00:41:26.420 --> 00:41:27.000
That's right.

00:41:27.540 --> 00:41:30.880
Everyone, until the police come,
can you stay in the rooms you were in?

00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:33.800
Don't go outside for any reason.

00:41:35.300 --> 00:41:36.220
I understand.

00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:41.180
Sakura-san,

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:43.980
was looking for something in
particular in this storage room,

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:45.560
when he was killed.

00:41:46.140 --> 00:41:47.100
But what on earth was it?

00:41:49.270 --> 00:41:51.650
The button on his coat looks like it was torn off.

00:41:52.280 --> 00:41:52.780
Yes.

00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:56.450
It seems like it was troublesome to unfasten them,

00:41:56.700 --> 00:41:59.320
but the wallet stuffed tightly with cash is safe.

00:42:00.700 --> 00:42:02.410
This isn't a robbery.

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:06.580
Don't touch the corpse!

00:42:06.790 --> 00:42:08.330
How many times do I have to
tell you until you understand?

00:42:10.670 --> 00:42:11.920
That hurts!

00:42:15.800 --> 00:42:16.260
Yes.

00:42:16.930 --> 00:42:18.890
I am Ayanokouji of the Kyoto Prefectural Police.

00:42:19.430 --> 00:42:21.970
Thank you very much for your efforts, please come in.

00:42:22.930 --> 00:42:23.720
You, stay outside.

00:42:23.970 --> 00:42:24.220
Yes.

00:42:27.770 --> 00:42:29.310
Inspector of the Kyoto Prefectural Police.

00:42:30.190 --> 00:42:31.610
You are remarkably fast in arriving.

00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:36.320
Did you bring your chipmunk today?

00:42:37.740 --> 00:42:39.700
I don't always take it with me.

00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:41.870
What do you think?

00:42:42.490 --> 00:42:43.790
Is it an external offender?

00:42:44.660 --> 00:42:46.000
I wouldn't say the possibility is zero.

00:42:46.790 --> 00:42:48.620
If the front door was opened, there would be a sound,

00:42:48.960 --> 00:42:50.250
and the okami would have noticed it.

00:42:51.170 --> 00:42:51.840
Moreover,

00:42:52.420 --> 00:42:53.670
the criminal knew that Sakura-san,

00:42:54.050 --> 00:42:56.970
would be in the storage room for whatever reason.

00:42:57.800 --> 00:42:58.300
In other words ...

00:42:59.010 --> 00:43:00.510
Sakura-san's acquaintances,

00:43:00.800 --> 00:43:02.390
Saijou-san, Ryuen-san,

00:43:02.390 --> 00:43:05.350
and Mizuo-san are the suspects.

00:43:06.600 --> 00:43:07.520
The three of them,

00:43:07.980 --> 00:43:10.150
after Sakura-san and Ran and them left,

00:43:10.650 --> 00:43:12.190
have each gotten up once to go to the restroom.

00:43:12.770 --> 00:43:13.190
Furthermore,

00:43:13.570 --> 00:43:15.780
there is a staircase that leads to the
basement on the way to the restroom.

00:43:16.860 --> 00:43:19.200
The three could have pretended to go to the restroom,

00:43:19.700 --> 00:43:21.990
and killed Sakura-san,

00:43:22.240 --> 00:43:24.120
who was in the storage room.

00:43:26.580 --> 00:43:28.290
One thing that concerns me is,

00:43:28.830 --> 00:43:30.670
when Mizuo-san went to the restroom,

00:43:31.120 --> 00:43:33.000
Chika Suzu-san followed him.

00:43:33.420 --> 00:43:33.920
Yes.

00:43:34.840 --> 00:43:36.550
All dancers do that.

00:43:37.210 --> 00:43:37.630
However,

00:43:37.880 --> 00:43:40.800
for Ryuen-san and Saijou-san, she didn't go.

00:43:41.340 --> 00:43:43.850
That was because she was playing a game with uncle.

00:43:44.300 --> 00:43:46.100
Conversely, the criminal may have aimed,

00:43:46.100 --> 00:43:48.220
for that chance and gotten up to go to the restroom.

00:43:48.600 --> 00:43:49.560
That means,

00:43:50.100 --> 00:43:52.150
Ryuen-san or Saijou-san is the criminal,

00:43:52.520 --> 00:43:53.770
and Mizuo-san is innocent.

00:43:54.310 --> 00:43:56.480
If Chika Suzu-san is not an accomplice ...

00:43:59.190 --> 00:43:59.690
That's right.

00:44:00.900 --> 00:44:01.660
Then let's go.

00:44:01.950 --> 00:44:02.280
Eh?

00:44:03.030 --> 00:44:04.200
Don't play dumb.

00:44:05.240 --> 00:44:07.910
That's why you searched Sakura-san's coat, right?

00:44:08.200 --> 00:44:08.700
Oh.

00:44:09.540 --> 00:44:10.370
You mean these?

00:44:11.330 --> 00:44:12.540
Sakura-san's shop was,

00:44:12.870 --> 00:44:14.460
on Teramachi Avenue, if I'm not mistaken.

00:44:12.870 --> 00:44:16.460
Note: "Teramachi" literally means "temple town"

00:44:15.130 --> 00:44:17.840
Sakura Antique Art Shop

00:44:26.430 --> 00:44:27.350
Yoshitsune Chronicles.

00:44:30.480 --> 00:44:31.270
Ise no Saburou!?

00:44:32.310 --> 00:44:32.850
Hattori!

00:44:37.070 --> 00:44:37.610
What?

00:44:38.230 --> 00:44:40.320
Sakura-san was Ise no Saburou!?

00:44:42.240 --> 00:44:42.860
What is this?

00:44:43.740 --> 00:44:44.860
T-This is ...

00:44:45.820 --> 00:44:46.740
A copy of the picture!

00:44:47.780 --> 00:44:48.700
What is the meaning of this?

00:44:49.290 --> 00:44:51.910
If Sakura-san had this picture ...

00:44:52.960 --> 00:44:56.290
Then he was the one who
delivered that letter to Sannou Temple.

00:44:57.630 --> 00:44:59.630
But, for what reason?

00:45:01.090 --> 00:45:01.800
What?

00:45:02.300 --> 00:45:03.880
Sakura-san was Ise no Saburou?

00:45:04.340 --> 00:45:04.720
Yes.

00:45:05.430 --> 00:45:07.640
That person was a member of the Genjibotaru group.

00:45:08.430 --> 00:45:09.260
Hold on,

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:13.230
Suruga no Jirou

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:13.230
Ise no Saburou

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:13.230
Bizen no
Heishirou

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:13.230
Kamei no
Rokurou

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:13.230
Washinoo no
Shichirou

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:13.230
Kataoka no
Hachirou

00:45:09.430 --> 00:45:11.350
so now the murdered victims are ...

00:45:12.270 --> 00:45:15.350
surely not me, whose name
possess the missing number five?

00:45:12.270 --> 00:45:15.350
Note: Mouri is referring to the numbers in the names of the Genjibotaru group.

00:45:13.230 --> 00:45:13.980
Suruga no Jirou

00:45:13.230 --> 00:45:13.980
Ise no Saburou

00:45:13.230 --> 00:45:13.980
