00:45:13.230 --> 00:45:13.980
Washinoo no
Shichirou

00:45:13.230 --> 00:45:13.980
Kataoka no
Hachirou

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:16.440
Suruga no Jirou

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:16.440
Ise no Saburou

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:16.440
Bizen no
Heishirou

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:16.440
Kamei no
Rokurou

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:16.440
Washinoo no
Shichirou

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:16.440
Kataoka no
Hachirou

00:45:14.560 --> 00:45:15.230
Mouri Kogorou

00:45:15.230 --> 00:45:16.440
Mouri Kogorou

00:45:16.860 --> 00:45:17.310
Ha?

00:45:18.020 --> 00:45:19.940
That happened a long time ago.

00:45:18.020 --> 00:45:21.940
Note: This is a reference to The Fourteenth Target, Detective Conan's second movie.

00:45:21.860 --> 00:45:25.070
If the picture at Sakura-san's was just a copy,

00:45:25.410 --> 00:45:27.660
and Sakura-san held onto the original,

00:45:27.990 --> 00:45:30.160
then didn't the criminal take that one?

00:45:30.450 --> 00:45:31.200
I see,

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:35.750
the criminal didn't think that
Sakura-san had taken a copy.

00:45:36.420 --> 00:45:36.880
Then,

00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:38.750
who's the real criminal?

00:45:39.670 --> 00:45:41.920
I think that it's either Ryuen-san, Saijou-san,

00:45:42.170 --> 00:45:44.920
Mizuo-san or Chika Suzu-san.

00:45:46.510 --> 00:45:49.050
But none of them had a weapon.

00:45:49.600 --> 00:45:51.390
After you guys slipped out,

00:45:51.640 --> 00:45:53.390
we inspected their bodies.

00:45:53.810 --> 00:45:55.640
Well, no one's stupid enough,

00:45:55.640 --> 00:45:57.900
to keep the weapon with him after he murders someone.

00:45:58.560 --> 00:46:00.570
He must have thrown it away or hid it somewhere.

00:46:01.020 --> 00:46:01.440
But,

00:46:01.900 --> 00:46:04.280
nothing was found inside of the store.

00:46:04.650 --> 00:46:05.740
How about from the Misogigawa?

00:46:06.360 --> 00:46:07.570
He could have thrown it away,

00:46:07.860 --> 00:46:09.570
from the glass window in the corridor of the basement.

00:46:09.780 --> 00:46:10.700
Don't you agree!?

00:46:11.160 --> 00:46:12.620
I thought so, too.

00:46:12.910 --> 00:46:13.160
Eh?

00:46:14.410 --> 00:46:15.160
Sonoko says,

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:18.960
that she heard something splash into the Misogigawa.

00:46:19.210 --> 00:46:19.710
Really?

00:46:20.130 --> 00:46:21.170
There's no mistake.

00:46:21.710 --> 00:46:22.340
But,

00:46:23.090 --> 00:46:24.960
the police searched the river,

00:46:25.260 --> 00:46:26.970
but they didn't find anything.

00:46:27.800 --> 00:46:29.760
It's strange ...

00:46:30.300 --> 00:46:31.890
there must've been an accomplice.

00:46:32.430 --> 00:46:35.640
The accomplice was outside and
grabbed the weapon out of the river.

00:46:35.890 --> 00:46:37.390
I don't think that's possible.

00:46:38.730 --> 00:46:39.690
Why do you think so, Ku—

00:46:39.770 --> 00:46:41.440
No, I mean Conan-kun.

00:46:42.400 --> 00:46:44.780
Tonight was a full moon, and it was bright outside.

00:46:45.570 --> 00:46:49.610
That balcony floor had gaps to be able to see below.

00:46:49.780 --> 00:46:52.120
Sakura Tea House

00:46:49.780 --> 00:46:52.120
Balcony

00:46:49.780 --> 00:46:52.120
Misogigawa

00:46:49.780 --> 00:46:52.120
Bank

00:46:50.410 --> 00:46:52.910
If there was an accomplice,

00:46:53.330 --> 00:46:55.160
Ran-neechan and everybody would have noticed him.

00:46:56.450 --> 00:46:57.370
Oh, right.

00:46:57.750 --> 00:46:58.920
The real situation was,

00:46:59.870 --> 00:47:01.330
that it was an outsider.

00:47:01.750 --> 00:47:03.840
Before Ran and everybody came out to the balcony,

00:47:04.420 --> 00:47:06.380
he sought entry through the basement's glass window,

00:47:07.050 --> 00:47:09.260
and hid in the bathroom.

00:47:10.010 --> 00:47:13.430
When Sakura-san came looking for
something in the storage room, he murdered him.

00:47:14.260 --> 00:47:16.390
And while still holding the weapon,

00:47:16.810 --> 00:47:18.640
he escaped from the glass window.

00:47:19.350 --> 00:47:21.690
But we didn't see anything,

00:47:22.400 --> 00:47:24.860
and there were no witnesses on the bank.

00:47:25.400 --> 00:47:26.480
It's just a coincidence.

00:47:27.030 --> 00:47:28.700
The murderer was lucky.

00:47:30.200 --> 00:47:32.070
Hmm, I'm not very satisfied with that explanation.

00:48:04.190 --> 00:48:05.770
That guy, he's the same one from Kuramayama.

00:48:19.620 --> 00:48:21.460
Kazuha, don't let go!

00:48:21.620 --> 00:48:22.420
What!?

00:48:35.600 --> 00:48:37.060
You stay here, alright!?

00:48:38.890 --> 00:48:39.390
Heiji!

00:48:56.700 --> 00:48:57.120
Hmph.

00:48:57.370 --> 00:48:58.830
You want to have a contest with me?

00:48:59.200 --> 00:48:59.910
Alright.

00:49:04.620 --> 00:49:06.080
What? There are gaps of opportunity everywhere.

00:49:11.340 --> 00:49:12.220
He's wearing kote?

00:49:12.220 --> 00:49:14.510
Note: "Kote" are gauntlets worn in kendo.

00:49:29.730 --> 00:49:32.110
Are you the one who murdered Sakura-san?

00:49:32.940 --> 00:49:36.280
If that's so, then do the same thing and slice me here!

00:50:10.570 --> 00:50:12.440
This isn't something that you'd want.

00:50:14.530 --> 00:50:16.110
Something's wrong with my eyes.

00:50:29.080 --> 00:50:30.670
Detective, over here, over here.

00:50:39.720 --> 00:50:41.100
Heiji? Are you alright?

00:50:41.600 --> 00:50:42.060
Kazuha ...

00:50:42.810 --> 00:50:43.510
The detective?

00:50:44.140 --> 00:50:45.770
It's a lie.

00:50:46.850 --> 00:50:49.400
Where did you learn to do that?

00:50:50.270 --> 00:50:51.560
You can be a terrible woman.

00:50:53.230 --> 00:50:53.860
Heiji!

00:50:58.030 --> 00:51:00.070
Umekouji Hospital

00:51:04.700 --> 00:51:05.950
Heiji, are you awake?

00:51:06.750 --> 00:51:07.410
Kazuha.

00:51:08.160 --> 00:51:08.960
We're glad you're alright.

00:51:09.250 --> 00:51:10.830
We were worried, Hei-chan.

00:51:13.170 --> 00:51:13.840
Ootaki-san ...

00:51:14.590 --> 00:51:16.130
And who was that again?

00:51:18.010 --> 00:51:19.380
I am Shiratori from police headquarters.

00:51:20.090 --> 00:51:21.970
I heard that the murdered Sakura Shouzou,

00:51:22.140 --> 00:51:23.850
was a member of the Genjibotaru group.

00:51:24.310 --> 00:51:25.430
I rushed from Tokyo.

00:51:26.720 --> 00:51:27.230
Does it hurt?

00:51:28.180 --> 00:51:29.020
Just a little.

00:51:29.600 --> 00:51:34.110
Stolen artifacts were found in Sakura's shop.

00:51:35.320 --> 00:51:36.570
Are you awake?

00:51:37.490 --> 00:51:39.030
Inspector, the short sword, did you ...

00:51:39.610 --> 00:51:41.160
We have turned it over to an expert.

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:43.950
Tell me as soon as the results come out.

00:51:44.330 --> 00:51:46.080
If there's not enough evidence,

00:51:47.370 --> 00:51:49.250
I'll offer this wound as evidence too.

00:51:49.660 --> 00:51:50.000
Eh?

00:51:50.370 --> 00:51:51.210
Evidence?

00:51:52.580 --> 00:51:56.550
Evidence that the short sword
was used to murder Sakura-san.

00:51:57.420 --> 00:51:59.630
It really would have been better if
we had something that the criminal,

00:51:59.760 --> 00:52:00.880
had touched with his skin.

00:52:01.680 --> 00:52:02.720
Ah, the motorcycle!

00:52:03.340 --> 00:52:04.430
There was a motorcycle, right?

00:52:04.600 --> 00:52:06.010
That was a stolen vehicle.

00:52:06.720 --> 00:52:08.390
Evidence that would specify the criminal?

00:52:12.190 --> 00:52:12.850
By the way,

00:52:14.150 --> 00:52:16.610
do you know what this picture is?

00:52:17.570 --> 00:52:19.900
It was held between the pages of
Sakura's Yoshitsune Chronicles.

00:52:21.990 --> 00:52:22.820
Are you sure?

00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:25.660
Very well.

00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:33.210
You should learn by this
experience and be obedient next time.

00:52:34.670 --> 00:52:35.920
With this, I must go as well.

00:52:37.500 --> 00:52:38.800
Take care, Hei-chan.

00:52:44.510 --> 00:52:46.600
I'm going to call my dad.

00:52:49.220 --> 00:52:50.770
Then I will ask the doctor ...

00:52:51.520 --> 00:52:52.060
Yes.

00:52:52.730 --> 00:52:53.900
Conan-kun is with me so—

00:52:53.900 --> 00:52:56.190
Ran-chan, I'm going out for a while,

00:52:56.440 --> 00:52:57.440
so look after Heiji for me.

00:53:10.160 --> 00:53:11.290
Are you going to be alright,

00:53:11.790 --> 00:53:12.830
not resting?

00:53:13.080 --> 00:53:13.870
I'm alright.

00:53:14.370 --> 00:53:16.420
Moreover, he was a really unusual guy.

00:53:17.380 --> 00:53:18.880
It's the first time I've seen that sort of style.

00:53:19.630 --> 00:53:22.510
Perhaps he had metal reinforcements
in his kote and was using it as a shield.

00:53:23.800 --> 00:53:26.970
I thought I'd get a comparison
of the weapon from my wound,

00:53:27.300 --> 00:53:29.390
so I made him get out his short
sword and wound me on purpose.

00:53:29.850 --> 00:53:31.680
But he left that sword behind.

00:53:32.310 --> 00:53:33.020
Why would he?

00:53:33.850 --> 00:53:34.560
Not only that,

00:53:35.190 --> 00:53:35.810
that guy,

00:53:36.560 --> 00:53:37.810
While we were fighting,

00:53:38.020 --> 00:53:40.730
tried to pick up the pouch I dropped.

00:53:41.110 --> 00:53:42.940
There are so many things I don't understand.

00:53:43.400 --> 00:53:46.990
You don't think that old man
might have been your first love?

00:53:47.280 --> 00:53:47.990
Hahaha!

00:53:48.120 --> 00:53:49.240
Right on the mark!

00:53:50.280 --> 00:53:51.120
Of course not!

00:53:51.410 --> 00:53:53.700
Mizuo Mansion

00:53:54.500 --> 00:53:56.620
You were attacked afterwards?

00:53:57.330 --> 00:53:58.830
I know it's impolite,

00:53:59.250 --> 00:54:01.170
but I came to ask if you had an alibi.

00:54:01.670 --> 00:54:02.710
In any case, the criminal,

00:54:03.090 --> 00:54:04.720
had on a Noh mask.

00:54:04.920 --> 00:54:05.970
A Noh mask?

00:54:06.680 --> 00:54:08.300
Because of that, may I ask if Saijou-san,

00:54:08.550 --> 00:54:11.010
and Ryuen-san have an alibi?

00:54:11.430 --> 00:54:12.600
Us too?

00:54:12.890 --> 00:54:14.140
This is unbearable.

00:54:14.520 --> 00:54:16.480
Today we came thinking,

00:54:16.810 --> 00:54:18.940
about conversing with Chika Suzu,

00:54:19.190 --> 00:54:20.730
about who the murderer of Sakura-san is.

00:54:21.230 --> 00:54:21.820
Right?

00:54:23.730 --> 00:54:24.240
It's alright.

00:54:24.820 --> 00:54:27.570
Last night I went straight
home from the tea house and slept.

00:54:28.240 --> 00:54:29.950
However, I'm single,

00:54:30.700 --> 00:54:32.660
and my room and my mother's room are separated,

00:54:33.160 --> 00:54:36.540
so I can't prove that I was home the whole time.

00:54:37.120 --> 00:54:38.870
I'm in the same situation.

00:54:39.330 --> 00:54:41.250
I live by myself on the second floor of my shop,

00:54:41.590 --> 00:54:42.880
on Teramachi Avenue.

00:54:43.500 --> 00:54:46.630
I read some Buddhist
scriptures in the main temple building,

00:54:47.090 --> 00:54:48.550
before I went to rest in my room.

00:54:49.340 --> 00:54:50.430
I don't have any witnesses.

00:54:50.890 --> 00:54:51.680
I see.

00:54:52.680 --> 00:54:53.560
One more thing,

00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:55.980
does everybody do archery?

00:54:56.730 --> 00:54:57.440
Archery?

00:54:57.850 --> 00:54:58.230
No.

00:54:58.690 --> 00:55:00.310
On the autumn-leaf viewing stage,

00:55:00.900 --> 00:55:04.570
Note: A bow made of a catalpa branch was a standard
implement used by shamanesses in Northeastern Japan.

00:55:00.900 --> 00:55:02.690
I do hold a catalpa bow.

00:55:03.440 --> 00:55:05.230
I've used the bow string balance,

00:55:05.690 --> 00:55:08.320
to ward off evil spirits, only on mere form.

00:55:08.860 --> 00:55:09.860
Then no one,

00:55:10.160 --> 00:55:12.370
that was there at the tea house that night,

00:55:12.780 --> 00:55:13.870
was skilled in archery?

00:55:14.790 --> 00:55:16.700
Which reminds me, Yamakura ...

00:55:18.460 --> 00:55:20.420
That Yamakura was doing archery?

00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:22.420
Yamakura Tae

00:55:20.960 --> 00:55:23.090
But she wasn't there at that time.

00:55:23.540 --> 00:55:24.210
Uh, no.

00:55:25.760 --> 00:55:26.590
Excuse me.

00:55:26.840 --> 00:55:27.880
Oh, you came.

00:55:29.380 --> 00:55:29.720
Eh?

00:55:30.010 --> 00:55:30.590
What's the matter?

00:55:30.930 --> 00:55:31.680
Come, come.

00:55:32.640 --> 00:55:33.930
Are you Chika Suzu-san?

00:55:34.140 --> 00:55:35.310
Yes, that's right.

00:55:35.810 --> 00:55:37.270
She surprised me because she looks different,

00:55:37.270 --> 00:55:38.350
from her dancing girl appearance.

00:55:38.770 --> 00:55:39.560
Come, please enter.

00:55:40.900 --> 00:55:41.230
Yes,

00:55:41.600 --> 00:55:42.310
Thank you.

00:55:54.160 --> 00:55:55.450
Thank you for last night.

00:55:55.740 --> 00:55:57.330
Please come again.

00:55:57.950 --> 00:55:59.000
It is I who should thank you.

00:56:02.420 --> 00:56:03.830
Thank you, goodbye.

00:56:05.540 --> 00:56:07.960
Sannouji was on Rokkaku avenue.

00:56:08.510 --> 00:56:10.550
This is Ebisu avenue, so ...

00:56:10.970 --> 00:56:14.220
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshi Oike.

00:56:14.680 --> 00:56:16.850
Ane-san Rokakku.

00:56:17.520 --> 00:56:18.890
It'll be the sixth one.

00:56:21.100 --> 00:56:25.730
Marutake Ebisu ni Oshi Oike.

00:56:27.320 --> 00:56:28.820
What was the song you just sang called?

00:56:29.110 --> 00:56:29.570
Well,

00:56:30.150 --> 00:56:33.410
Note: "Temari" is a traditional Japanese handball game.

00:56:30.150 --> 00:56:32.410
we just call it a temari song.

00:56:34.410 --> 00:56:36.410
It's about Kyoto's roads that run East and West,

00:56:36.700 --> 00:56:38.740
and they're sung in the order of North to South.

00:56:39.620 --> 00:56:43.540
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshi Oike.

00:56:43.960 --> 00:56:48.050
Ane-san Rokakku Tako Nishiki.

00:56:48.630 --> 00:56:52.590
Shi Aya Bu Taka Matsu Man Gojyou.

00:56:52.930 --> 00:56:56.430
Setta Chara Chara Uonotana.

00:56:52.930 --> 00:56:56.430
Sandals, "Crack Crack", fish rack

00:56:56.930 --> 00:57:00.930
Rokujyou Hijyou Toorisugi,

00:56:56.930 --> 00:57:00.930
Pass the sixth and seventh,

00:57:01.430 --> 00:57:05.400
Hachijyou Koereba Touji Michi.

00:57:01.430 --> 00:57:05.400
And if you pass the eighth, you'll be at Touji road.

00:57:05.900 --> 00:57:09.940
Kujyou Oujite Todomesasu.

00:57:05.900 --> 00:57:09.940
And the end is at the ninth.

00:57:11.490 --> 00:57:15.780
All the children of Kyoto learn
the names of the roads by this song.

00:57:17.240 --> 00:57:19.910
Then does that mean you're from Kyoto as well?

00:57:20.580 --> 00:57:21.620
Yes, that's right.

00:57:21.950 --> 00:57:22.500
And your age?

00:57:22.710 --> 00:57:23.710
Nineteen.

00:57:24.040 --> 00:57:24.670
Nineteen?

00:57:30.840 --> 00:57:32.300
This is Oike avenue.

00:57:33.340 --> 00:57:34.630
Then I will leave from here.

00:57:36.840 --> 00:57:37.720
Goodbye.

00:57:38.100 --> 00:57:38.680
Goodbye.

00:57:40.220 --> 00:57:41.890
Do you think she is ...

00:57:42.270 --> 00:57:43.100
There's no mistake,

00:57:43.640 --> 00:57:46.810
she's from Kyoto and she's two years older than me.

00:57:47.270 --> 00:57:48.060
But,

00:57:48.360 --> 00:57:50.320
all the children in Kyoto have ...

00:57:50.400 --> 00:57:52.110
Finally I was able to meet her, finally.

00:57:54.110 --> 00:57:54.990
Yes. Hello.

00:57:55.030 --> 00:57:56.360
Hei-chan, what are you doing?

00:57:57.030 --> 00:57:59.070
You can't just jump out the hospital on your own.

00:57:59.410 --> 00:58:00.490
Ah, Ootaki-san.

00:58:00.620 --> 00:58:04.580
Kyoto Prefectural Police

00:58:01.200 --> 00:58:02.370
Well, leaving that,

00:58:02.870 --> 00:58:04.620
the test results are in.

00:58:05.830 --> 00:58:07.790
It was from the hilt of the short sword.

00:58:08.130 --> 00:58:12.250
The same blood type of Sakura-san's was detected,

00:58:12.840 --> 00:58:17.010
and the impression on
Sakura-san's wound matched as well.

00:58:17.260 --> 00:58:17.970
Is that true?

00:58:18.550 --> 00:58:18.970
Hei-chan,

00:58:19.470 --> 00:58:20.640
I'll say this just in case,

00:58:21.010 --> 00:58:22.180
but don't be rash.

00:58:22.930 --> 00:58:24.390
If something ever happened to you,

00:58:24.850 --> 00:58:26.100
how will I ever explain it to your father?

00:58:26.440 --> 00:58:27.650
Alright, I understand.

00:58:27.940 --> 00:58:29.270
Thanks, Ootaki-han.

00:58:35.740 --> 00:58:37.990
Now we know that the old masked man that attacked me,

00:58:38.320 --> 00:58:41.450
is the same person that murdered Sakura-san.

00:58:41.910 --> 00:58:42.790
Then,

00:58:43.160 --> 00:58:46.000
the four people that were unable to dispose the weapon,

00:58:46.580 --> 00:58:48.420
are not suspects anymore.

00:59:04.270 --> 00:59:06.640
Conan-kun! What are you doing?

00:59:08.140 --> 00:59:09.480
You guys! Why?

00:59:09.690 --> 00:59:11.150
As a reward for answering Professor's quiz,

00:59:11.440 --> 00:59:13.070
he took us along.

00:59:13.440 --> 00:59:14.860
However, Genta-kun ...

00:59:15.360 --> 00:59:16.650
He got lost.

00:59:16.990 --> 00:59:17.700
Ah!

00:59:18.740 --> 00:59:20.280
Well then, use the detective badges.

00:59:20.660 --> 00:59:23.280
We've already called him and made contact,

00:59:23.870 --> 00:59:24.330
but ...

00:59:24.580 --> 00:59:26.370
Genta-kun can't read kanji,

00:59:26.660 --> 00:59:28.160
so he can't tell where he is right now.

00:59:28.660 --> 00:59:32.210
We thought you could find him
by using those glasses of yours.

00:59:32.630 --> 00:59:33.250
Okay.

00:59:33.590 --> 00:59:34.590
Leave it to me.

00:59:36.170 --> 00:59:37.090
Oh!

00:59:37.420 --> 00:59:37.880
Hey!

00:59:38.170 --> 00:59:40.050
This is interesting. Oh! He's over there!

00:59:41.140 --> 00:59:41.640
Jeez ...

00:59:53.020 --> 00:59:55.150
There seems to be a case over here, too.

00:59:55.860 --> 00:59:56.320
Yeah.

00:59:56.730 --> 00:59:58.320
I'll tell you the details later.

00:59:59.900 --> 01:00:00.530
Hold on ...

01:00:00.950 --> 01:00:02.410
Ai-kun the drug please.

01:00:08.870 --> 01:00:09.460
What's that?

01:00:09.790 --> 01:00:11.540
A drug that suppresses growling stomachs.

01:00:12.000 --> 01:00:14.420
Professor developed it for
ceremonies and special occasions.

01:00:15.040 --> 01:00:17.250
Plus, other drugs for people who are weak with alcohol,

01:00:17.420 --> 01:00:20.090
and some others that turn
your face red right after you take it.

01:00:20.380 --> 01:00:23.340
Also, I developed drugs for people
who want to take a day off from work,

01:00:23.340 --> 01:00:25.140
which gives you the same symptoms as a cold.

01:00:26.430 --> 01:00:28.600
I got help from Ai while developing all the drugs.

01:00:28.970 --> 01:00:30.600
None of them seem to be of any use to me.

01:00:30.680 --> 01:00:34.690
Rokakku Building

01:00:31.690 --> 01:00:32.770
Oh, right here, right here.

01:00:33.060 --> 01:00:34.400
He's in this Rokakku building.

01:00:35.520 --> 01:00:36.360
He's here?

01:00:37.860 --> 01:00:38.730
That's good.

01:00:39.230 --> 01:00:40.240
Mom ...

01:00:40.400 --> 01:00:41.990
Ah, there he is!

01:00:43.780 --> 01:00:44.780
I'm saved.

01:00:45.070 --> 01:00:46.620
We're glad you're okay, Genta-kun!

01:00:46.910 --> 01:00:49.410
I thought we'd never meet for a lifetime.

01:00:49.500 --> 01:00:50.450
Me too!

01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:52.460
Nevertheless, that's pretty convenient.

01:00:54.080 --> 01:00:56.540
A badge with a transmitter.

01:00:57.000 --> 01:00:57.710
Yes.

01:00:58.090 --> 01:01:00.260
The frequency waves that the badge transmits,

01:01:00.590 --> 01:01:02.220
synchronizes with these glasses and ...

01:01:03.760 --> 01:01:04.260
Hattori!

01:01:04.390 --> 01:01:05.140
Oh, that's how!

01:01:05.930 --> 01:01:06.760
Wh-what!?

01:01:08.220 --> 01:01:09.720
Kudou, you don't think ...

01:01:18.110 --> 01:01:19.320
There's no mistake.

01:01:21.070 --> 01:01:22.570
The sound that girl heard was,

01:01:23.150 --> 01:01:25.030
the sound of the weapon hitting the water.

01:01:25.740 --> 01:01:26.410
Then,

01:01:26.740 --> 01:01:28.660
the suspect is among the four people there.

01:01:29.330 --> 01:01:30.450
No, among the three.

01:01:31.370 --> 01:01:34.460
There's no way that my first love is the murderer, right?

01:01:34.790 --> 01:01:35.540
Hey, hey.

01:01:36.210 --> 01:01:38.840
There's only one thing that concerns me.

01:01:39.170 --> 01:01:42.170
Between the song that we just
heard and the song I remember,

01:01:42.460 --> 01:01:43.590
there's one part that's different.

01:01:44.760 --> 01:01:46.010
My first love sang,

01:01:46.390 --> 01:01:49.850
the part of "Ane-san Rokakku" as "Yome-san Rokakku".

01:01:49.850 --> 01:01:53.100
Note: "Yome" means bride. "Ane" means older sister.

01:01:51.520 --> 01:01:52.810
I wonder why ...

01:01:53.430 --> 01:01:54.020
How would I know?

01:02:08.410 --> 01:02:09.160
I found it!

01:02:09.450 --> 01:02:10.490
The fragment of the mask!

01:02:20.880 --> 01:02:21.630
Hmm ...

01:02:21.630 --> 01:02:22.130
Inspector!

01:02:23.300 --> 01:02:24.800
What's the groaning about?

01:02:25.220 --> 01:02:25.720
This is...?

01:02:27.130 --> 01:02:30.350
The three members who were
murdered in Tokyo wore them.

01:02:31.010 --> 01:02:34.810
One wore the hat, another wore the
scarf, and the other wore the gloves.

01:02:35.310 --> 01:02:37.190
The color, design and material are all the same.

01:02:37.850 --> 01:02:39.350
Don't you think it's strange?

01:02:39.940 --> 01:02:41.190
Yes, you're right.

01:02:42.110 --> 01:02:42.940
Why? What's strange?

01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:43.860
For example,

01:02:44.400 --> 01:02:46.950
if Shiratori-kun wore all three items,

01:02:47.320 --> 01:02:48.740
It isn't unusual. However,

01:02:49.530 --> 01:02:51.070
if Inspector Megure had the hat,

01:02:51.740 --> 01:02:52.910
I had the scarf,

01:02:53.490 --> 01:02:55.250
and Takagi-kun had on the gloves,

01:02:55.540 --> 01:02:56.500
something would be strange, right?

01:02:57.000 --> 01:02:57.870
That's for sure.

01:02:58.830 --> 01:03:00.790
It seems as though Shiratori-san had died,

01:03:01.000 --> 01:03:03.460
and divided his belongings between us.

01:03:05.260 --> 01:03:05.960
That's it!

01:03:06.840 --> 01:03:07.880
Wh-What?

01:03:11.260 --> 01:03:12.220
I'm hungry.

01:03:12.300 --> 01:03:13.470
Be patient.

01:03:14.010 --> 01:03:17.230
Chika Suzu-san's mother was a
young geisha in Miyagawachou,

01:03:17.940 --> 01:03:19.770
and passed away due to illness when she was five.

01:03:20.850 --> 01:03:22.190
Her mother was not married.

01:03:23.110 --> 01:03:26.690
Chika Suzu-san was taken in and
raised by the mistress of a tea house,

01:03:27.110 --> 01:03:28.280
Yamakura Tae.

01:03:28.650 --> 01:03:30.570
What does unwed mother mean?

01:03:31.160 --> 01:03:32.160
Well that is ...

01:03:32.490 --> 01:03:35.580
A woman who didn't marry but had a child.

01:03:36.370 --> 01:03:38.870
We don't know who her father is.

01:03:39.330 --> 01:03:41.380
However, there is an anonymous payment,

01:03:41.380 --> 01:03:42.580
sent to the tea house every month.

01:03:43.380 --> 01:03:43.790
But,

01:03:44.170 --> 01:03:45.500
for some reason, three months ago,

01:03:45.880 --> 01:03:47.420
the payment stopped.

01:03:49.420 --> 01:03:52.090
It certainly does seem like a worrisome account.

01:03:52.970 --> 01:03:54.510
Three months ago?

01:03:55.850 --> 01:03:58.270
But Inspector Shiratori,
where did you get such information?

01:03:58.980 --> 01:04:00.730
You heard it from the Royal Inspector right?

01:04:00.940 --> 01:04:01.900
That's wrong.

01:04:02.520 --> 01:04:07.110
Note: Gion is the entertainment district of Kyoto.

01:04:02.520 --> 01:04:05.730
Even if it doesn't look it, I am a
known face in the Gion district.

01:04:06.440 --> 01:04:06.860
Heh,

01:04:07.110 --> 01:04:07.940
Is that a boast?

01:04:08.650 --> 01:04:09.360
Generally,

01:04:09.740 --> 01:04:11.860
even if they say he is my rival,

01:04:12.410 --> 01:04:15.280
don't compare me with someone
who always takes his chipmunk.

01:04:15.280 --> 01:04:16.160
A chipmunk?

01:04:16.290 --> 01:04:16.660
Yes.

01:04:17.120 --> 01:04:18.450
He has it in his pocket.

01:04:18.750 --> 01:04:21.790
As one would expect, he left it
when he came to the scene of the crime.

01:04:22.250 --> 01:04:22.960
A chipmunk ...

01:04:25.090 --> 01:04:26.670
Yes, this is Shiratori.

01:04:27.300 --> 01:04:28.010
This is Megure.

01:04:28.510 --> 01:04:30.130
About Yoshitsune and Benkei,

01:04:30.380 --> 01:04:31.880
there may be one possibility ...

01:04:33.050 --> 01:04:33.890
Distribution of mementos?

01:04:34.340 --> 01:04:36.180
If we think about it that way, the mystery can be solved.

01:04:36.810 --> 01:04:37.390
In other words,

01:04:37.760 --> 01:04:42.600
either Yoshitsune or Benkei has
already died. That's what we reasoned.

01:04:44.480 --> 01:04:45.900
I get it!

01:04:56.530 --> 01:04:57.080
Mouri-san,

01:04:57.780 --> 01:05:01.000
you said you know who
murdered Sakura-san, is this really true?

01:05:01.410 --> 01:05:01.870
Yes.

01:05:04.460 --> 01:05:05.830
Well then, please allow me to tell you.

01:05:06.380 --> 01:05:07.340
The culprit is ...

01:05:07.670 --> 01:05:08.460
Chika Suzu-san ...

01:05:09.050 --> 01:05:09.670
It's you!

01:05:10.710 --> 01:05:11.590
That's absurd!

01:05:13.090 --> 01:05:14.590
Your reasoning is off.

01:05:15.220 --> 01:05:16.390
Is he alright?

01:05:16.470 --> 01:05:18.260
Anyhow, let's hear him out until the end.

01:05:20.220 --> 01:05:23.310
The motive is revenge for the murder of your father,

01:05:23.520 --> 01:05:27.690
who is the leader of the robbery group, Yoshitsune.

01:05:29.570 --> 01:05:33.700
Yoshitsune was betrayed by his
servants and murdered three months ago.

01:05:34.150 --> 01:05:36.280
That's why the payments to the tea house stopped.

01:05:37.030 --> 01:05:37.700
I see ...

01:05:38.910 --> 01:05:40.830
Plus, you had an accomplice.

01:05:41.580 --> 01:05:42.290
Benkei.

01:05:42.870 --> 01:05:43.540
Benkei?

01:05:44.210 --> 01:05:46.040
As to Benkei, who is it?

01:05:46.830 --> 01:05:47.630
The Royal Inspector!

01:05:48.250 --> 01:05:49.090
It's you!

01:05:51.630 --> 01:05:52.670
Chika Suzu-san,

01:05:52.970 --> 01:05:56.390
when you came to the tea
house, you secretly brought something.

01:05:56.890 --> 01:06:00.720
The short sword and the inspector's chipmunk!

01:06:04.180 --> 01:06:05.020
How cute!

01:06:05.600 --> 01:06:08.270
That chipmunk was the key to the trick.

01:06:08.690 --> 01:06:09.730
Chika Suzu-san,

01:06:09.940 --> 01:06:15.360
Note: Zashiki is a Japanese tatami room.

01:06:09.940 --> 01:06:13.440
You gave the appearance of going to
the restroom on the way to the zashiki,

01:06:13.690 --> 01:06:15.360
and murdered Sakura-san in the storage room.

01:06:16.030 --> 01:06:19.030
Then you tied the short sword to the
chipmunk you had hidden in a cupboard,

01:06:19.320 --> 01:06:22.620
and let it escape from the basement's glass window.

01:06:23.500 --> 01:06:26.870
The chipmunk jumped into
Misogigawa and made for the bank.

01:06:28.330 --> 01:06:31.340
That's where the Inspector was waiting to pick them up.

01:06:31.630 --> 01:06:34.590
Later, he tried to murder Heiji with the short sword.

01:06:35.260 --> 01:06:35.970
I get it!

01:06:36.220 --> 01:06:39.300
So the sound I heard was the
chipmunk jumping into the water!

01:06:40.010 --> 01:06:43.020
Besides Sakura-san's murder, you
two are involved in the other cases.

01:06:43.810 --> 01:06:46.100
Inspector, do you do archery?

01:06:46.600 --> 01:06:49.150
Do I look like I've done anything that complicated?

01:06:49.600 --> 01:06:51.360
Is that really true?

01:06:52.770 --> 01:06:54.190
However, Chika Suzu-san,

01:06:54.690 --> 01:06:55.820
I hear that people,

01:06:56.070 --> 01:06:58.990
who do archery have an injury
here where the arrowhead scraped.

01:06:59.990 --> 01:07:00.820
Certainly,

01:07:01.450 --> 01:07:04.910
I injured my "yanomakura" due to archery, but,

01:07:07.660 --> 01:07:09.250
I just started.

01:07:09.540 --> 01:07:11.750
There's no way I could shoot anyone.

01:07:12.340 --> 01:07:13.840
I think so, too.

01:07:14.340 --> 01:07:17.170
If you injure that spot, it's proof that you're a beginner.

01:07:17.670 --> 01:07:20.140
That's what I heard my
acquaintances from the archery club say.

01:07:20.760 --> 01:07:23.640
And if there was murder, the
distribution of the mementos ...

01:07:24.140 --> 01:07:25.430
Mouri-han!

01:07:25.560 --> 01:07:28.520
Do you really think this girl is the culprit!?

01:07:28.810 --> 01:07:29.900
Therefore, I ...

01:07:29.900 --> 01:07:31.270
Enough joking around!

01:07:31.610 --> 01:07:34.860
Dancers are busy performing and entertaining guests,

01:07:35.150 --> 01:07:37.490
there is no time for them to be murdering people!

01:07:37.780 --> 01:07:38.530
Hey, hey.

01:07:38.950 --> 01:07:39.450
What is it?

01:07:39.910 --> 01:07:40.950
About the chipmunk ...

01:07:41.240 --> 01:07:44.160
With a small body like that, I don't
think it could carry a short sword.

01:07:45.120 --> 01:07:45.830
Shut up!

01:07:46.450 --> 01:07:48.160
Then I'll show you the proof!

01:07:51.120 --> 01:07:53.000
C'mon, move chipmunk!

01:07:53.670 --> 01:07:55.460
I am too shocked to be able to speak.

01:07:56.250 --> 01:07:59.720
You're purposefully ignoring me
in order to be free from guilt, huh?

01:08:01.890 --> 01:08:02.970
Stop it!

01:08:03.050 --> 01:08:05.640
Don't you feel sorry for it!?

01:08:06.060 --> 01:08:07.770
It's animal cruelty!

01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:09.890
You kids shut up!

01:08:10.140 --> 01:08:11.940
Genta-kun, save the chipmunk!

01:08:12.060 --> 01:08:12.600
Oh.

01:08:13.810 --> 01:08:14.190
Kudou.

01:08:15.570 --> 01:08:16.110
Yeah.

01:08:16.820 --> 01:08:19.070
Thanks to uncle, I know who the culprit is.

01:08:20.110 --> 01:08:20.650
Same here.

01:08:21.450 --> 01:08:24.570
Only those who do archery would say that.

01:08:25.280 --> 01:08:26.660
What's left is the evidence ...

01:08:28.250 --> 01:08:29.750
And the location of the Buddhist statue.

01:08:30.410 --> 01:08:32.540
Poor chipmunk.

01:08:33.040 --> 01:08:34.840
Let's give it something to eat!

01:08:35.340 --> 01:08:37.800
I have some acorns ...

01:08:42.800 --> 01:08:47.060
Note: A Japanese children song about an acorn that falls into a puddle.

01:08:42.800 --> 01:08:45.100
It's almost like the song, "Donguri Koro Koro"

01:08:45.680 --> 01:08:46.680
Donguri Koro Koro?

01:08:48.270 --> 01:08:49.100
Perhaps ...

01:08:54.230 --> 01:08:55.730
Hey! What's the matter, Kudou?

01:08:56.020 --> 01:09:00.820
Perhaps the copied picture concerned the roads of Kyoto.

01:09:01.150 --> 01:09:01.820
What?

01:09:05.910 --> 01:09:07.330
First are the roads that run East to West.

01:09:08.290 --> 01:09:09.410
The fifth row stands for,

01:09:09.790 --> 01:09:12.500
Gojyou Avenue

01:09:10.370 --> 01:09:12.040
Note: "Gojyou" means fifth.

01:09:10.370 --> 01:09:11.040
"Gojyou Avenue".

01:09:12.250 --> 01:09:13.040
The fourth row,

01:09:12.620 --> 01:09:15.960
Shijyou Avenue

01:09:13.960 --> 01:09:15.790
Note: "Shijyou" means fourth.

01:09:13.960 --> 01:09:14.790
is "Shijyou Avenue".

01:09:15.750 --> 01:09:17.670
And in between the third and second row,

01:09:18.000 --> 01:09:19.800
which means between 2nd and 3rd Avenue,

01:09:19.840 --> 01:09:23.180
Oike Avenue

01:09:20.300 --> 01:09:22.220
Note: "Oike" is literally the "honourable lake."

01:09:20.300 --> 01:09:21.090
is "Oike Avenue".

01:09:22.420 --> 01:09:23.340
And to prove it,

01:09:24.800 --> 01:09:26.010
Donguri Koro Koro?

01:09:27.510 --> 01:09:28.850
Next are the roads that run North to South.

01:09:29.680 --> 01:09:33.850
Note: Literally "The Spring River". It is also a traditional Japanese
childrens song which tells about a river in the spring that blooms with violets.

01:09:29.680 --> 01:09:31.850
The violet, which is present in the song "Haru no Ogawa",

01:09:31.430 --> 01:09:33.850
Ogawa Avenue

01:09:32.480 --> 01:09:33.230
is part of "Ogawa Avenue".

01:09:34.140 --> 01:09:37.310
Note: "Karasuma" is literally "crow circle".

01:09:34.140 --> 01:09:36.860
The Tengu or "Crow billed Tengu" is
represented in "Karasuma Avenue".

01:09:34.980 --> 01:09:37.270
Karasuma Avenue

01:09:37.400 --> 01:09:39.860
Fuji-san → Tomi

01:09:37.770 --> 01:09:38.730
And for Mt. Fuji,

01:09:39.650 --> 01:09:42.150
Note: "Tominokouji" literally means "wealthy, small road"

01:09:39.650 --> 01:09:41.650
the character "fu" is "tomi".
So it is "Tominokouji Avenue".

01:09:39.860 --> 01:09:42.190
Tominokouji Avenue

01:09:42.990 --> 01:09:44.240
What is the chicken for?

01:09:44.780 --> 01:09:46.620
Note: "Yana gawa nabe" is a sort of soup prepared with loach.

01:09:44.780 --> 01:09:46.530
The loach has something to do with "Yana gawa nabe",

01:09:46.740 --> 01:09:49.160
Yanaginobanba Avenue

01:09:46.950 --> 01:09:49.160
Note: Yanaginobanba literally means "Horse willow place".

01:09:46.950 --> 01:09:48.870
so it must represent "Yanaginobanba Avenue".

01:09:49.660 --> 01:09:50.700
The chicken is ...

01:09:52.410 --> 01:09:53.870
Nishinotouin Avenue!

01:09:54.330 --> 01:09:57.380
Chicken → West

01:09:54.330 --> 01:09:57.380
Nishinotouin Avenue

01:09:54.660 --> 01:09:56.830
The character for chicken is
similar to the character for west.

01:09:57.580 --> 01:09:59.130
Well that's pretty hard.

01:10:00.630 --> 01:10:02.340
Then what does this one mean?

01:10:05.340 --> 01:10:08.470
For the cicada, there's an "abura semi",
which relates to "Aburanokouji Avenue".

01:10:06.930 --> 01:10:08.640
Aburanokouji Avenue

01:10:08.890 --> 01:10:10.510
The Tengu represents "Karasuma Avenue".

01:10:09.300 --> 01:10:10.430
Karasuma Avenue

01:10:11.060 --> 01:10:12.100
And if the goldfish,

01:10:12.560 --> 01:10:14.520
Note: "Fu" is literally wheat bran.

01:10:12.560 --> 01:10:14.520
has something to do with goldfish food "fu",

01:10:13.310 --> 01:10:15.730
Fuyachou Avenue

01:10:14.810 --> 01:10:15.890
it represents "Fuyachou Avenue".

01:10:16.480 --> 01:10:19.060
Then if you connect the
similarly colored violet and Mt. Fuji,

01:10:19.690 --> 01:10:21.860
the chicken and loach, the cicada and goldfish,

01:10:22.150 --> 01:10:23.740
and both tengu's together in a line ...

01:10:24.740 --> 01:10:25.200
"King".

01:10:26.110 --> 01:10:27.200
Why is it a king?

01:10:30.280 --> 01:10:30.740
It's a dot!

01:10:31.700 --> 01:10:32.240
Isn't it like this?

01:10:34.870 --> 01:10:38.630
Tama → Gyoku

01:10:35.960 --> 01:10:37.290
Tama can also be read as gyoku,

01:10:37.580 --> 01:10:38.580
or jewels.

01:10:38.630 --> 01:10:41.090
Bukkou Temple

01:10:40.000 --> 01:10:40.710
This place is ...

01:10:42.340 --> 01:10:43.130
Bukkou Temple!

01:10:44.130 --> 01:10:46.340
It's the same as if we found the treasure!

01:11:05.570 --> 01:11:06.190
What's wrong?

01:11:07.070 --> 01:11:07.530
Nothing.

01:11:08.320 --> 01:11:09.280
I just feel a little dizzy.

01:11:09.530 --> 01:11:11.830
Rokakku Building

01:11:14.790 --> 01:11:15.830
Sorry, thanks.

01:11:16.410 --> 01:11:17.750
How do you feel now?

01:11:18.580 --> 01:11:18.960
Yes.

01:11:19.870 --> 01:11:20.920
I feel better.

01:11:22.170 --> 01:11:22.790
Hattori.

01:11:23.500 --> 01:11:24.340
Eight years ago,

01:11:24.750 --> 01:11:27.050
the temple you snuck into was Sannou Temple.

01:11:28.050 --> 01:11:28.930
How did you know that!?

01:11:29.760 --> 01:11:30.300
Idiot.

01:11:30.680 --> 01:11:33.470
While you were admiring the
Sakura blossoms, it came to me.

01:11:34.220 --> 01:11:36.980
Also, there was the latticed window you talked about.

01:11:39.060 --> 01:11:39.560
That's right.

01:11:40.350 --> 01:11:43.060
I picked up this crystal ball under the Sakura tree.

01:11:44.440 --> 01:11:45.940
I'm sorry to throw water onto things,

01:11:46.320 --> 01:11:47.440
but that crystal ball,

01:11:47.900 --> 01:11:50.740
wasn't dropped by your first love.

01:11:51.820 --> 01:11:52.620
What?

01:11:53.410 --> 01:11:54.030
Actually ...

01:11:54.830 --> 01:11:56.240
It's from the stolen Buddhist statue.

01:11:56.240 --> 01:11:58.870
Note: Byakugou is the crystal ball just between the eyes.

01:11:56.240 --> 01:11:58.660
It's Sannou Temple's "crystal ball",
which was inserted in its forehead.

01:11:56.540 --> 01:11:59.040
Byakugou

01:11:59.580 --> 01:12:00.290
Crystal ball?

01:12:00.830 --> 01:12:04.670
Is that the thing that's in the
Buddha's brow which releases light?

01:12:05.170 --> 01:12:05.710
Yes.

01:12:06.500 --> 01:12:09.260
In Buddhist statues it's
frequently represented as a crystal ball.

01:12:10.300 --> 01:12:11.300
It's the same in Noh masks.

01:12:13.180 --> 01:12:14.600
My reasoning is this.

01:12:15.140 --> 01:12:17.720
Eight years ago, the robbery group Genjibotaru,

01:12:18.480 --> 01:12:20.310
snuck into the main hall of Sannou Temple,

01:12:20.890 --> 01:12:22.690
and stole the treasured Buddhist statue.

01:12:26.570 --> 01:12:30.110
However, while taking it away, the byakugou fell out.

01:12:37.540 --> 01:12:39.410
When the leader, Yoshitsune, noticed it later,

01:12:39.910 --> 01:12:42.540
he sent one of his servants to Sannou Temple to find it.

01:12:43.000 --> 01:12:43.920
It was then that ...

01:12:56.760 --> 01:12:58.470
I want to eat some zenzai!

01:12:58.520 --> 01:13:00.640
Note: Anmitsu is syrup covered bean jam.

01:12:58.520 --> 01:12:59.890
I want anmitsu!

01:13:02.810 --> 01:13:04.560
Reluctantly, the leader stored the Buddhist statue,

01:13:04.560 --> 01:13:06.770
in the storage room of Sakura-san's shop.

01:13:07.480 --> 01:13:08.480
And eight years later,

01:13:08.900 --> 01:13:13.660
the culprit found out that the
boy from eight years ago was you.

01:13:14.200 --> 01:13:15.280
It was that magazine!

01:13:19.160 --> 01:13:22.080
Around the same time, there was an
event that occurred in the robbery group.

01:13:22.620 --> 01:13:25.630
Perhaps the leader became seriously ill or something.

01:13:26.250 --> 01:13:27.540
The leader, who felt his time was near,

01:13:28.000 --> 01:13:31.420
hid the stolen Buddhist statue in another location.

01:13:32.130 --> 01:13:35.510
He gave each of his servants a
picture that held the location of it,

01:13:36.720 --> 01:13:39.310
and left a will saying whoever
was to find the Buddhist statue,

01:13:39.310 --> 01:13:40.470
would become the new leader.

01:13:42.730 --> 01:13:44.520
Then he died.

01:13:45.230 --> 01:13:46.810
The remaining servants,

01:13:47.110 --> 01:13:49.820
tried earnestly to solve the mystery, but were unable to.

01:13:50.440 --> 01:13:50.980
Around that time ...

01:13:51.730 --> 01:13:53.740
As Sakura-san was one of the members,

01:13:54.110 --> 01:13:55.910
he came to the culprit to join arms.

01:13:56.950 --> 01:13:59.410
Sakura-san knew his skill as a swordsman,

01:13:59.700 --> 01:14:02.620
and tried to goad him into killing the other members.

01:14:03.040 --> 01:14:03.870
Then,

01:14:05.080 --> 01:14:07.670
they'd find the location of the
Buddhist statue and its Byakugou,

01:14:07.960 --> 01:14:10.300
and split the money made from selling the statue.

01:14:12.380 --> 01:14:13.050
Perhaps,

01:14:13.420 --> 01:14:16.590
within the robbery group,
Sakura-san, the owner of an antique art shop,

01:14:17.140 --> 01:14:19.800
was the only one who had seized the sale
and distribution routes of the black market.

01:14:20.560 --> 01:14:23.430
He probably felt he was the only one who was safe.

01:14:24.180 --> 01:14:26.770
The culprit acted as if he agreed to Sakura-san's plan,

01:14:27.270 --> 01:14:29.400
when his true feelings were to
murder all the members of the group,

01:14:29.520 --> 01:14:31.270
and monopolize the treasure.

01:14:32.320 --> 01:14:36.700
But in order to do that, he had to
solve the mystery left by the leader.

01:14:34.400 --> 01:14:37.490
Bukkou Temple

01:14:38.070 --> 01:14:39.120
So the culprit thought ...

01:14:39.240 --> 01:14:42.990
to ask the famous detective, Mouri
Kogorou to solve the mystery for him.

01:14:44.910 --> 01:14:45.750
Bukkou Temple ...

01:14:46.290 --> 01:14:46.830
It's right here.

01:14:49.500 --> 01:14:52.750
But is the Buddhist statue really hidden here?

01:14:53.000 --> 01:14:55.260
Yeah, something doesn't seem right.

01:14:56.130 --> 01:14:56.800
H-hey!

01:14:59.680 --> 01:15:00.350
Hey, what's the matter?

01:15:00.890 --> 01:15:01.390
Hey Kudou!

01:15:01.720 --> 01:15:02.890
What have you found?

01:15:04.930 --> 01:15:05.390
This is ...

01:15:05.230 --> 01:15:09.600
Stone: "Jewel Dragon Temple Remains"

01:15:10.020 --> 01:15:10.810
Jewel Dragon Temple?

01:15:11.270 --> 01:15:12.690
The dot on the picture pointed to this?

01:15:13.020 --> 01:15:13.530
Yes.

01:15:15.990 --> 01:15:16.490
It's Kazuha.

01:15:16.950 --> 01:15:17.450
It's me.

01:15:17.860 --> 01:15:19.160
I have the girl in my custody.

01:15:19.950 --> 01:15:20.700
In an hour,

01:15:21.320 --> 01:15:23.370
come alone to the Jewel Dragon Temple in Kuramayama.

01:15:24.040 --> 01:15:25.370
If you contact the police,

01:15:25.660 --> 01:15:26.830
the girl will die.

01:15:27.460 --> 01:15:28.540
Heiji, don't come!

01:15:28.750 --> 01:15:29.620
You'll be killed!

01:15:30.120 --> 01:15:30.630
Kazuha!

01:15:30.920 --> 01:15:31.460
Kazuha!

01:15:32.630 --> 01:15:33.210
Hattori?

01:15:33.920 --> 01:15:34.590
Kazuha was ...

01:15:35.050 --> 01:15:36.460
Kazuha was kidnapped.

01:15:36.710 --> 01:15:37.130
What!?

01:15:37.550 --> 01:15:41.340
In an hour I was told to go alone
to Gyokuryu Temple in Kuramayama.

01:15:41.840 --> 01:15:42.640
Gyokuryu Temple!

01:15:46.520 --> 01:15:47.600
Well, isn't that good?

01:15:48.690 --> 01:15:50.350
We can break in there together and ...

01:15:55.280 --> 01:15:55.820
Hattori!

01:15:56.730 --> 01:15:59.820
Return Bridge

01:16:00.030 --> 01:16:04.030
"When the child that heard of his father's death from afar, rushed to Kyoto."

01:16:04.030 --> 01:16:07.370
"The funeral procession was just going over this bridge."

01:16:07.370 --> 01:16:11.040
"In that moment, the father temporarily revived,"

01:16:11.040 --> 01:16:14.540
"and the father and child exchanged words."

01:16:17.670 --> 01:16:18.210
Hello.

01:16:20.590 --> 01:16:23.180
Kuramayama

01:16:23.430 --> 01:16:26.350
Gyokuryu Temple

01:16:38.150 --> 01:16:39.070
It's the teacher's will.

01:16:39.440 --> 01:16:40.740
Put the "Underworld Katana" in Benkei's drawer,

01:16:40.950 --> 01:16:42.820
and put the bow in Rokakku's drawer.

01:16:43.780 --> 01:16:46.450
Um, Benkei's drawer is ...

01:16:47.580 --> 01:16:49.080
From the top, one, two, three ...

01:16:50.410 --> 01:16:53.370
I wonder what those are, the
Benkei and Rokakku drawers ...

01:16:54.460 --> 01:16:55.290
Bukkou Temple?

01:16:56.340 --> 01:16:58.420
I heard them talking about it, but ...

01:17:04.720 --> 01:17:07.430
Really, where have those two gone?

01:17:07.930 --> 01:17:10.560
Even if I call Kazuha's cell phone, she isn't answering.

01:17:11.680 --> 01:17:12.480
Gyokuryu Temple?

01:17:12.770 --> 01:17:14.230
I'm hungry!

01:17:14.400 --> 01:17:16.270
Is that so? Then once we get back ...

01:17:16.310 --> 01:17:17.110
Excuse me.

01:17:18.020 --> 01:17:19.190
This Gyokuryu Temple,

01:17:19.730 --> 01:17:20.990
where is it now?

01:17:21.070 --> 01:17:22.990
It's back deep in Kuramayama.

01:17:23.490 --> 01:17:26.820
But I heard that it was evacuated a long time ago.

01:17:27.580 --> 01:17:28.280
Thank you.

01:17:30.830 --> 01:17:31.830
Kuramayama?

01:17:41.260 --> 01:17:42.010
He's late.

01:17:42.880 --> 01:17:45.800
Knowing that it's a trap, no one will come that easily.

01:17:46.300 --> 01:17:47.260
Do you really think so?

01:17:47.930 --> 01:17:50.350
Maybe the wind of cowardice blew in his direction.

01:17:55.310 --> 01:17:56.020
Heiji!

01:18:10.450 --> 01:18:10.990
You!

01:18:11.830 --> 01:18:13.500
You didn't hurt Kazuha, did you?

01:18:15.160 --> 01:18:16.710
I'm alright, Heiji.

01:18:17.380 --> 01:18:19.130
What you really wanted,

01:18:19.500 --> 01:18:20.090
was this.

01:18:24.470 --> 01:18:26.680
In order to get back this crystal ball,

01:18:27.140 --> 01:18:29.510
you attacked me yesterday on this mountain.

01:18:29.890 --> 01:18:31.430
Looks like you failed, though.

01:18:32.390 --> 01:18:35.020
Next, you thought you'd monopolize the treasure,

01:18:35.270 --> 01:18:38.190
so you attacked Sakura-san
at the tea house in Hontochou.

01:18:39.020 --> 01:18:42.360
It wasn't Giyon or Miyagawachou because,

01:18:42.980 --> 01:18:45.950
the tea house in Hontochou has a river flowing behind it.

01:18:46.400 --> 01:18:46.990
River?

01:18:47.490 --> 01:18:50.950
After you murdered Sakura-san
who was searching the storage room,

01:18:51.700 --> 01:18:55.410
you put a terminal that security
companies use for thefts and lost individuals,

01:18:55.660 --> 01:18:57.960
along with the weapon in a
plastic bottle and threw it out.

01:19:00.710 --> 01:19:02.420
Then later, with a cell phone,

01:19:02.920 --> 01:19:05.340
you accessed the security company's website,

01:19:05.720 --> 01:19:08.090
to find the location of the
terminal, which you then recovered.

01:19:08.890 --> 01:19:09.930
After that,

01:19:10.180 --> 01:19:12.390
you waited in ambush with your
motorcycle for me, who was returning to Osaka,

01:19:12.680 --> 01:19:14.560
And tried to kill me with the same short sword.

01:19:17.980 --> 01:19:21.020
This attempt was thwarted
because of Kazuha's intervention.

01:19:21.310 --> 01:19:23.070
But you purposefully dropped the short sword,

01:19:23.070 --> 01:19:24.730
in order to be removed from being a suspect.

01:19:24.900 --> 01:19:26.110
The culprit wanted to make us believe,

01:19:26.240 --> 01:19:28.700
That it was someone who had
escaped with the weapon from the tea house.

01:19:29.070 --> 01:19:29.910
Isn't that right?

01:19:30.320 --> 01:19:31.320
Saijou Taiga-san.

01:19:31.740 --> 01:19:35.080
Or should I say Musashibou Benkei.

01:19:41.130 --> 01:19:43.540
As one would expect from the
high school detective from Osaka,

01:19:43.880 --> 01:19:44.920
Hattori Heiji.

01:19:45.760 --> 01:19:47.550
How did you know it was me?

01:19:47.840 --> 01:19:51.010
You tried to hide that you did archery.

01:19:51.800 --> 01:19:53.100
When you sat down,

01:19:53.600 --> 01:19:55.810
you drew back your right foot halfway before sitting.

01:19:56.100 --> 01:20:00.390
Note: "Hansoku wo Hiku" means To pull foot halfway.

01:19:56.390 --> 01:19:58.100
That's called "hansoku wo hiku".

01:19:58.350 --> 01:20:01.270
People who do archery sometimes do it out of habit.

01:20:02.020 --> 01:20:02.650
Also,

01:20:03.190 --> 01:20:06.110
when asked if you did any
archery, you thoughtlessly started to say,

01:20:06.320 --> 01:20:07.860
"Yamakura".

01:20:09.200 --> 01:20:10.910
Which reminds me, Yamakura ...

01:20:11.740 --> 01:20:14.410
You weren't talking about
Yamakura-san of the tea house,

01:20:14.700 --> 01:20:15.540
but of "Ya no makura"

01:20:15.950 --> 01:20:17.580
When you draw an arrow, you place the arrow,

01:20:17.950 --> 01:20:21.000
on the second joint of the thumb on the left hand.

01:20:22.080 --> 01:20:24.290
Perhaps you tried to say it like this.

01:20:24.670 --> 01:20:29.050
Which reminds me, Chika
Suzu-san had an injury on her "yamakura".

01:20:29.880 --> 01:20:33.800
Only people who do archery would know a term like that.

01:20:34.970 --> 01:20:37.350
By the way, Ryuen-san is an amateur in archery.

01:20:37.100 --> 01:20:39.930
Note: The character for bow string is "gen" or "tsuru"

01:20:37.220 --> 01:20:40.180
Gen  =  Tsuru

01:20:37.810 --> 01:20:40.100
He called the bow string, "gen" instead of "tsuru."

01:20:42.440 --> 01:20:45.520
I attended the town's kendo
gym with Ryuen and everybody.

01:20:46.110 --> 01:20:47.650
But one day,

01:20:48.070 --> 01:20:51.450
I learned that there was an old
technique in Kyoto, a "Yoshitsune style".

01:20:52.150 --> 01:20:54.780
I studied the "Yoshitsune-style" by myself,

01:20:55.490 --> 01:20:57.870
And two years ago, I stopped attending the kendo gym.

01:20:58.370 --> 01:21:01.120
Then personally called myself the
successor of the Yoshitsune style.

01:21:01.750 --> 01:21:03.330
Benkei, the successor of the Yoshitsune style.

01:21:04.290 --> 01:21:08.300
I ... I liked Yoshitsune more
than Benkei from the beginning.

01:21:08.670 --> 01:21:10.210
I wanted to become Yoshitsune!

01:21:11.920 --> 01:21:12.630
However,

01:21:12.970 --> 01:21:14.590
the leader took the title of Yoshitsune,

01:21:14.970 --> 01:21:16.930
and I, who stood at the top of the robbery group,

01:21:17.350 --> 01:21:20.140
was given the name of Benkei.

01:21:20.810 --> 01:21:23.100
The reason you tried to monopolize the Buddhist statue,

01:21:23.520 --> 01:21:24.350
was it for money?

01:21:24.810 --> 01:21:26.810
That's right, but it wasn't for personal desire.

01:21:27.610 --> 01:21:30.190
It was to make a dojo here.

01:21:30.650 --> 01:21:33.240
This temple was where the leader was the chief priest.

01:21:33.610 --> 01:21:36.660
Even after it was evacuated,
it was supervised by the leader,

01:21:37.330 --> 01:21:40.450
and I used it as a place to practice the Yoshitsune style.

01:21:41.330 --> 01:21:43.790
But the leader died three months ago,

01:21:44.170 --> 01:21:45.710
and the temple was going to be taken down.

01:21:47.000 --> 01:21:49.630
I wasn't going to be able to use it as a dojo!

01:21:50.250 --> 01:21:51.760
There's one thing I wanted to ask.

01:21:52.510 --> 01:21:54.630
You just took advantage of Ryuen-san.

01:21:55.380 --> 01:21:56.050
That's right.

01:21:56.340 --> 01:21:58.640
I heard him talking about the statue some time ago,

01:21:59.220 --> 01:22:01.310
and when I sent that letter to Sannou Temple.

01:22:02.020 --> 01:22:03.640
Sure enough, he came to discuss it with me.

01:22:04.560 --> 01:22:05.140
So,

01:22:05.600 --> 01:22:08.560
I set him up to send a request to Mouri Kogorou.

01:22:10.270 --> 01:22:11.780
I killed Sakura-san,

01:22:11.980 --> 01:22:15.950
because I could find someone
to purchase the Buddhist statue.

01:22:16.820 --> 01:22:20.580
Now there's something convenient called the Internet.

01:22:20.910 --> 01:22:21.540
Come.

01:22:21.910 --> 01:22:23.290
Chatting time is over.

01:22:23.750 --> 01:22:25.670
Hand over the crystal ball!

01:22:26.250 --> 01:22:28.130
In exchange for it, let Kazuha go!

01:22:28.330 --> 01:22:29.170
That's fine ...

01:22:29.670 --> 01:22:32.090
If you tell me where the statue's hidden.

01:22:32.460 --> 01:22:33.010
What?

01:22:33.880 --> 01:22:34.420
Well ...

01:22:34.970 --> 01:22:35.970
Where is the statue?

01:22:36.760 --> 01:22:37.840
It's in this temple.

01:22:38.260 --> 01:22:39.140
What are you saying?

01:22:39.550 --> 01:22:42.060
Note: This is a Japanese idiom, and it's like... Is it
that you can't see what you already have in front of you?

01:22:39.550 --> 01:22:41.260
Is it that you can't see the forest because of the trees?

01:22:41.720 --> 01:22:42.520
You're lying!

01:22:42.930 --> 01:22:44.640
I've already searched this temple!

01:22:44.890 --> 01:22:45.560
There's no ...

01:22:45.690 --> 01:22:46.640
It's not a lie!

01:23:03.240 --> 01:23:04.250
Kazuha! Run!

01:23:05.450 --> 01:23:06.000
Heiji!

01:23:25.060 --> 01:23:26.430
They're my disciples.

01:23:27.140 --> 01:23:28.600
You guys stay out of it!

01:23:35.320 --> 01:23:35.940
Heiji!

01:23:40.240 --> 01:23:40.870
Stop it!

01:23:41.120 --> 01:23:42.580
This person isn't Heiji!

01:23:51.290 --> 01:23:52.590
Wh-who?

01:23:53.380 --> 01:23:54.800
Who are you!?

01:23:55.880 --> 01:23:57.210
Kudou Shinichi.

01:23:59.430 --> 01:24:00.220
A detective.

01:24:01.050 --> 01:24:01.680
What?

01:24:02.640 --> 01:24:03.350
What?

01:24:03.760 --> 01:24:05.140
You let him take the medicine?

01:24:06.430 --> 01:24:07.680
Kudou-kun called.

01:24:08.020 --> 01:24:11.980
He asked if there was a way to
return to Kudou Shinichi once more,

01:24:12.060 --> 01:24:12.900
Even temporarily.

01:24:13.690 --> 01:24:14.110
But,

01:24:14.610 --> 01:24:17.940
there isn't any more of the trial antidote to APTX 4869.

01:24:18.860 --> 01:24:20.530
And before, even the Paical,

01:24:20.910 --> 01:24:22.620
which he drank as a cold
medicine and returned to his original body,

01:24:23.280 --> 01:24:25.200
is ineffective as he has created an antibody to it.

01:24:26.330 --> 01:24:27.660
Then it occurred to me ...

01:24:28.750 --> 01:24:31.750
If he took the medicine that
gave you symptoms of a severe cold,

01:24:32.330 --> 01:24:34.170
and drank the Paical one more time,

01:24:35.500 --> 01:24:39.090
he might be able to return to his original body.

01:24:39.760 --> 01:24:40.930
So then ...

01:24:42.550 --> 01:24:44.760
As I thought, the experiment was a huge success.

01:24:45.390 --> 01:24:47.600
Kudou-kun returned to his original body.

01:24:48.520 --> 01:24:51.060
However, it's the same as having a severe cold.

01:24:51.270 --> 01:24:52.310
His body is shaky.

01:24:52.770 --> 01:24:54.360
I can't guarantee his life.

01:24:54.730 --> 01:24:56.480
And how is Heiji-kun feeling?

01:24:56.980 --> 01:24:57.610
Who knows?

01:24:58.030 --> 01:25:01.360
Until he undergoes examination tomorrow, he must rest.

01:25:01.860 --> 01:25:04.700
For the time being, I've been
assigned the role to keep guard.

01:25:13.250 --> 01:25:14.000
Kudou-kun?

01:25:17.500 --> 01:25:17.960
Damn.

01:25:18.750 --> 01:25:19.880
You've deceived me.

01:25:30.020 --> 01:25:31.680
I thought that somehow I'd be
able to at least let her escape,

01:25:32.310 --> 01:25:33.730
But my body won't move the way I want.

01:25:37.230 --> 01:25:40.070
This is dangerous, the effect of the Paical is wearing off.

01:25:42.780 --> 01:25:43.400
I'm done for!

01:25:46.320 --> 01:25:48.740
For a detective, you'd be the best in the world.

01:25:49.870 --> 01:25:51.000
But as a samurai,

01:25:51.830 --> 01:25:52.910
You're not very good.

01:25:53.540 --> 01:25:54.120
Hattori!

01:25:54.460 --> 01:25:55.040
Heiji!

01:25:55.420 --> 01:25:56.460
I made you wait, Kazuha.

01:25:57.380 --> 01:25:59.420
What do you mean, making me wait? You idiot!

01:25:59.500 --> 01:26:00.710
What were you doing until now?

01:26:04.090 --> 01:26:04.720
Hey Kudou!

01:26:06.890 --> 01:26:08.720
You seem to have snatched my clothes.

01:26:09.470 --> 01:26:10.100
Also,

01:26:10.850 --> 01:26:12.180
I don't know what you painted on your face,

01:26:12.640 --> 01:26:14.440
But I'm not this dark-colored.

01:26:14.850 --> 01:26:15.440
Really?

01:26:16.060 --> 01:26:16.730
That's alright.

01:26:17.060 --> 01:26:18.270
I'll take it from here.

01:26:18.650 --> 01:26:19.360
You hurry and go!

01:26:20.070 --> 01:26:21.940
Hide before you become small.

01:26:22.650 --> 01:26:24.240
And when you return to normal, come back.

01:26:27.990 --> 01:26:28.780
Wait there!

01:26:29.160 --> 01:26:30.700
Your opponent is me!

01:26:33.540 --> 01:26:34.080
Kazuha,

01:26:34.460 --> 01:26:36.080
Don't tell anyone you met Kudou here,

01:26:37.120 --> 01:26:38.080
even to that girl.

01:26:38.380 --> 01:26:39.290
Eh? Even to Ran-chan?

01:26:39.340 --> 01:26:39.960
Why?

01:26:40.460 --> 01:26:41.340
Just because.

01:26:42.340 --> 01:26:43.510
They probably won't meet anyways.

01:26:44.470 --> 01:26:45.760
It's better she doesn't know.

01:26:50.640 --> 01:26:53.100
I won't allow you two to return alive.

01:26:56.850 --> 01:26:58.350
This sword is too weak.

01:27:02.610 --> 01:27:03.190
After them!

01:27:07.490 --> 01:27:08.450
Hey, did you find him?

01:27:08.910 --> 01:27:09.570
No, not yet.

01:27:09.910 --> 01:27:10.620
Search harder!

01:27:12.200 --> 01:27:12.700
What?

01:27:13.790 --> 01:27:14.910
Shh, be quiet.

01:27:15.450 --> 01:27:16.160
Don't move.

01:27:28.130 --> 01:27:29.050
Shinichi!

01:27:29.640 --> 01:27:30.720
You have the same expression.

01:27:31.640 --> 01:27:32.260
Like that time.

01:27:34.470 --> 01:27:35.310
What happened?

01:27:36.270 --> 01:27:37.520
You're covered in sweat.

01:27:38.100 --> 01:27:39.060
And those people ...

01:27:39.730 --> 01:27:40.650
Who are they?

01:27:45.440 --> 01:27:46.320
Where did he go?

01:27:46.610 --> 01:27:47.860
It can't be helped, let's go back.

01:27:50.200 --> 01:27:51.030
I'm sorry Ran.

01:27:51.780 --> 01:27:53.160
Right now, to meet with you, I ...

01:28:12.550 --> 01:28:14.680
It's been locked, the door won't open.

01:28:15.100 --> 01:28:15.890
Do something!

01:28:16.770 --> 01:28:19.100
Note: Tatami are Japanese floor coverings, woven out of straw.

01:28:16.770 --> 01:28:17.890
The smell of this tatami ...

01:28:18.520 --> 01:28:20.140
It's the room that I was pushed into.

01:28:22.440 --> 01:28:24.060
Bring me the axe, hurry!

01:28:24.650 --> 01:28:25.230
Damn!

01:28:25.820 --> 01:28:27.690
It's only a matter of time until they break in.

01:28:28.360 --> 01:28:30.450
Is there anything that can be used as a weapon ...

01:28:34.700 --> 01:28:35.330
What is this?

01:28:36.080 --> 01:28:37.790
This chest has a large amount of drawers.

01:28:39.370 --> 01:28:39.870
Ah!

01:28:40.370 --> 01:28:41.670
Put the "Underworld Katana" in Benkei's drawer,

01:28:42.080 --> 01:28:44.000
And the bow and arrows in Rokakku's drawer.

01:28:44.710 --> 01:28:45.090
Heiji!

01:28:45.630 --> 01:28:47.710
The sword is in Benkei's drawer.

01:28:47.920 --> 01:28:48.380
What?

01:28:48.840 --> 01:28:49.670
In this chest?

01:28:51.130 --> 01:28:55.220
But there are so many. How
am I to know which one is his?

01:29:05.440 --> 01:29:07.520
I feel like I've seen this before.

01:29:09.570 --> 01:29:12.570
The beams of these drawers,
aren't they like the roads of Kyoto?

01:29:21.330 --> 01:29:22.000
I get it.

01:29:22.660 --> 01:29:25.630
This beam is Karasuma Avenue
and this one Takoyakushi Avenue.

01:29:26.500 --> 01:29:27.000
Hold on ...

01:29:28.050 --> 01:29:31.550
Could it be the names of drawers
are taken from the names of places?

01:29:32.130 --> 01:29:32.760
The names of places?

01:29:35.510 --> 01:29:36.260
That's it!

01:29:36.800 --> 01:29:38.010
Rokakku means Rokakku Hall.

01:29:39.220 --> 01:29:41.140
Benkei's drawer means ...

01:29:43.600 --> 01:29:44.940
Benkei's Stone!

01:29:44.810 --> 01:29:46.020
Sanjou Avenue

01:29:45.520 --> 01:29:47.190
Going East from Sanjou to Fuyachou.

01:29:46.150 --> 01:29:47.310
Fuyachou Avenue

01:29:47.770 --> 01:29:48.520
It's the temari song!

01:29:49.270 --> 01:29:51.360
Hmm ... Marutake Ebisu Ni ...

01:29:52.820 --> 01:29:54.150
Marutake Ebisu Ni ...

01:29:55.070 --> 01:29:56.370
What was after that?

01:29:58.530 --> 01:29:59.410
Ah, damn!

01:29:59.830 --> 01:30:00.830
I can't remember!

01:30:00.120 --> 01:30:03.830
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshi Oike.

01:30:04.500 --> 01:30:08.250
Yome-san Rokakku Tako Nishiki.

01:30:08.880 --> 01:30:10.840
Heiji! Sanjyou is two before Tako.

01:30:12.420 --> 01:30:14.380
Two above Tako, and the road that runs West to East is ...

01:30:15.010 --> 01:30:16.260
Temple then ... Fuya ...

01:30:16.930 --> 01:30:18.010
Fuyachou is the third one!

01:30:18.640 --> 01:30:19.140
It's right here!

01:30:21.930 --> 01:30:22.810
Be prepared!

01:30:39.530 --> 01:30:41.790
The equal sides of this unique blade ...

01:30:43.080 --> 01:30:44.500
It's the demon sword "Muramasa"!

01:30:47.120 --> 01:30:49.630
It's just right for cutting monsters,

01:30:49.960 --> 01:30:51.460
That have possessed Yoshitsune.

01:30:51.920 --> 01:30:52.590
What did you say!?

01:30:55.090 --> 01:30:56.380
Get out of the way!

01:31:01.970 --> 01:31:02.930
What are you doing!?

01:31:03.310 --> 01:31:04.390
Hurry and go after them!

01:31:04.520 --> 01:31:05.230
Yes.

01:31:09.150 --> 01:31:10.940
Alright, I'm going to delay them.

01:31:11.230 --> 01:31:12.650
Meanwhile, you escape.

01:31:13.150 --> 01:31:13.650
No!

01:31:14.030 --> 01:31:15.030
I want to be with ...

01:31:15.740 --> 01:31:16.900
Listen to me!

01:31:18.030 --> 01:31:18.610
Heiji.

01:31:18.990 --> 01:31:19.570
He's here!

01:31:20.570 --> 01:31:21.330
Hurry, go!

01:31:27.210 --> 01:31:27.870
You guys,

01:31:28.120 --> 01:31:29.370
After the girl!

01:31:41.220 --> 01:31:41.890
Conan-kun!

01:31:42.300 --> 01:31:43.010
Kazuha-neechan,

01:31:43.640 --> 01:31:44.520
What about Heiji-niisan?

01:31:49.390 --> 01:31:50.060
Over there!

01:31:50.690 --> 01:31:51.310
Hattori!

01:31:56.820 --> 01:31:57.530
Damn!

01:31:57.990 --> 01:32:00.570
I want to inform the police, but my
cell phone doesn't have any reception.

01:32:02.320 --> 01:32:02.820
That's it!

01:32:20.430 --> 01:32:21.890
Hey, put it out immediately.

01:32:22.390 --> 01:32:22.930
Yes.

01:32:25.350 --> 01:32:27.720
Alright, now if someone notices this fire ...

01:32:28.560 --> 01:32:29.020
Hey.

01:32:29.600 --> 01:32:30.390
Hey Ran.

01:32:33.650 --> 01:32:34.570
Are you awake?

01:32:35.150 --> 01:32:35.980
Dad!

01:32:39.070 --> 01:32:39.780
Where's Shinichi?

01:32:39.950 --> 01:32:42.030
What? Are you still half asleep?

01:32:42.570 --> 01:32:44.070
Why would he be here?

01:32:44.780 --> 01:32:47.370
More importantly, why are you sleeping here?

01:32:47.790 --> 01:32:50.000
And you Dad, what are you doing here?

01:32:50.040 --> 01:32:51.160
I notified him,

01:32:51.920 --> 01:32:54.380
About Kazuha being kidnapped by the Genjibotaru group.

01:32:54.630 --> 01:32:55.090
Mouri-san!

01:33:09.810 --> 01:33:12.020
It's about time to come to a conclusion.

01:33:14.730 --> 01:33:15.900
As you wish!

01:33:21.740 --> 01:33:23.530
You aren't going to trick me again.

01:33:24.280 --> 01:33:24.820
Then,

01:33:25.570 --> 01:33:26.280
How about this?

01:33:27.450 --> 01:33:28.080
A short sword!

01:33:28.950 --> 01:33:30.500
It's not an ordinary short sword.

01:33:31.200 --> 01:33:33.710
There's a deadly poison with
immediate results painted on it.

01:33:35.040 --> 01:33:35.710
What did you say?

01:33:36.080 --> 01:33:38.550
Just a little scratch and you're dead.

01:33:41.010 --> 01:33:42.590
What a coward!

01:34:09.740 --> 01:34:11.240
Oh no! Heiji's in danger!

01:34:11.540 --> 01:34:13.040
You can't run away anymore.

01:34:13.790 --> 01:34:15.750
From below, the arrows are aimed at you.

01:34:21.630 --> 01:34:22.510
Something has to be done.

01:34:24.050 --> 01:34:24.680
Conan-kun!?

01:34:24.840 --> 01:34:25.430
Wait there!

01:34:29.850 --> 01:34:31.220
Hey! Over here!

01:34:40.820 --> 01:34:44.950
utsumuku sono senaka ni

01:34:40.820 --> 01:34:44.950
On your stooping back.

01:34:44.950 --> 01:34:48.530
itai ame ga tsuki sasaru

01:34:44.950 --> 01:34:48.530
The painful rain sticks.

01:34:46.570 --> 01:34:47.660
Take this!

01:34:48.740 --> 01:34:55.160
inoru omoide mite ita

01:34:48.740 --> 01:34:55.160
I watched you with praying thoughts.

01:34:55.540 --> 01:34:59.500
kono yo ni moshimo kasa ga

01:34:55.540 --> 01:34:59.500
In this world, if there was.

01:34:56.460 --> 01:34:57.750
Go Hattori!

01:34:57.920 --> 01:34:58.750
Heiji!

01:34:59.670 --> 01:35:03.170
tatta hitotsu da to shite mo

01:34:59.670 --> 01:35:03.170
Only one umbrella.

01:35:03.340 --> 01:35:10.140
sagashite kimi ni watasu yo

01:35:03.340 --> 01:35:10.140
I will find it and hand it to you.

01:35:10.300 --> 01:35:14.180
nanimo dekinai kedo

01:35:10.300 --> 01:35:14.180
I can't do anything but,

01:35:14.350 --> 01:35:17.310
kimi no kawari

01:35:14.350 --> 01:35:17.310
If it's for you.

01:35:17.310 --> 01:35:24.740
nureru kurai wake mo nai sa~

01:35:17.310 --> 01:35:24.740
Becoming wet is nothing at all.

01:35:24.940 --> 01:35:28.860
onegai sono nayami wo

01:35:24.940 --> 01:35:28.860
Please, take those worries.

01:35:27.320 --> 01:35:29.450
The Benkei who wanted to become Yoshitsune.

01:35:28.860 --> 01:35:36.540
douka watashi ni uchiakete

01:35:28.860 --> 01:35:36.540
And open your heart to me.

01:35:30.240 --> 01:35:31.580
If you were Benkei,

01:35:31.950 --> 01:35:34.370
Yoshitsune would have been
killed at the Ataka checkpoint.

01:35:35.450 --> 01:35:36.710
The leader's been defeated!

01:35:53.180 --> 01:35:54.180
Arrest them all!

01:35:54.350 --> 01:35:54.850
Yes.

01:35:55.520 --> 01:35:56.810
It turned out good, Conan-kun!

01:35:56.980 --> 01:35:57.430
Yes!

01:35:58.140 --> 01:36:01.900
Japanese culture: You usually affix -san after
the last name. It's like the "Mr." in Mr. Smith.

01:35:58.140 --> 01:36:01.350
But back there, you addressed Heiji as Hattori.

01:36:01.560 --> 01:36:03.650
Sorry, I just got caught up in the excitement.

01:36:04.190 --> 01:36:04.780
It's Heiji!

01:36:05.400 --> 01:36:06.070
Heiji!

01:36:10.410 --> 01:36:11.160
This temple ...

01:36:21.370 --> 01:36:23.130
Now all the mysteries are solved.

01:36:26.710 --> 01:36:30.430
It seems like the effect of the drug was only temporary.

01:36:31.130 --> 01:36:31.640
Well,

01:36:31.890 --> 01:36:34.640
Thanks to you, I was able to collect some valuable data.

01:36:37.270 --> 01:36:38.640
Are you alright, Heiji?

01:36:38.890 --> 01:36:39.770
Yes, one way or another.

01:36:40.140 --> 01:36:42.440
But where is the Buddhist statue?

01:36:42.900 --> 01:36:43.520
Ahem.

01:36:47.480 --> 01:36:48.610
Hattori-kun, Shin ...

01:36:49.990 --> 01:36:50.900
Hm? What?

01:36:51.530 --> 01:36:52.910
No, nothing.

01:36:54.700 --> 01:36:56.740
Of course, that was only a dream.

01:37:19.930 --> 01:37:21.730
Sannou Temple — Early Morning

01:37:22.190 --> 01:37:23.650
I am truly ashamed that I was not able,

01:37:24.150 --> 01:37:26.270
to ascertain the location of the Buddhist statue.

01:37:26.770 --> 01:37:27.400
No,

01:37:27.900 --> 01:37:30.780
this is what Buddha has chosen.

01:37:31.530 --> 01:37:32.990
Do not worry about it.

01:37:33.740 --> 01:37:35.990
Everyone, please be careful.

01:37:38.620 --> 01:37:39.290
Goodbye.

01:37:47.670 --> 01:37:48.840
But this is worrisome,

01:37:49.420 --> 01:37:52.380
there is only one hour left until the
unveiling of the Buddhist statue.

01:37:53.090 --> 01:37:53.880
It's alright,

01:37:54.380 --> 01:37:56.220
we'll just proceed as usual.

01:38:04.640 --> 01:38:06.690
The ... The Healing Buddha!

01:38:07.440 --> 01:38:09.190
He has returned!

01:38:11.360 --> 01:38:13.650
Gyokuryu Temple — Early Dawn

01:38:20.660 --> 01:38:21.700
It's here, Kudou.

01:38:22.330 --> 01:38:23.750
See, it's just as I said.

01:38:28.250 --> 01:38:30.800
Well, I never thought that the
shape of the temple would be "tama",

01:38:31.460 --> 01:38:33.380
and the position of the dot indicated the bell tower.

01:38:35.300 --> 01:38:37.840
Even I didn't notice that ...

01:38:37.800 --> 01:38:41.600
Note: "tama" means ball and "takara" means treasure.

01:38:37.840 --> 01:38:41.600
Note: A "ukanmuri" is the sort of roof style thing that you see in the explanation.

01:38:37.890 --> 01:38:41.810
Tama

01:38:38.260 --> 01:38:39.970
If you put an "ukanmuri" on the top of "tama",

01:38:39.140 --> 01:38:41.810
Takara

01:38:40.390 --> 01:38:41.470
it becomes "treasure".

01:38:42.350 --> 01:38:44.480
The ukanmuri represented a roof.

01:38:45.100 --> 01:38:46.270
I see ...

01:38:54.900 --> 01:38:56.200
Now it's back to normal.

01:38:56.860 --> 01:38:57.320
Yes.

01:39:01.410 --> 01:39:03.870
Those two are a good combination.

01:39:04.700 --> 01:39:07.120
Almost like Yoshitsune and Benkei.

01:39:09.460 --> 01:39:12.170
Do you mean that boy Hattori
and the famous detective Mouri?

01:39:13.000 --> 01:39:15.630
You still have some way to go in your training ...

01:39:16.010 --> 01:39:18.390
Ha ha ha.

01:39:21.100 --> 01:39:21.720
Well now ...

01:39:25.730 --> 01:39:26.230
Alright,

01:39:26.520 --> 01:39:28.230
Ayumi-chan you're next.

01:39:30.110 --> 01:39:31.520
It's so cute!

01:39:32.070 --> 01:39:33.820
Maybe I should take it home!

01:39:33.860 --> 01:39:34.730
That's too bad.

01:39:35.190 --> 01:39:36.860
It's my number one friend.

01:39:37.570 --> 01:39:41.200
Inspector, could it be that you
don't have many human friends?

01:39:43.330 --> 01:39:46.200
I'm sorry I called both of you the culprits.

01:39:46.960 --> 01:39:47.870
That's alright.

01:39:48.500 --> 01:39:51.330
To tell the truth, I knew who my father was.

01:39:51.630 --> 01:39:55.050
I told him myself that it was
alright not to send me any more money.

01:39:55.710 --> 01:39:57.340
Y-Your father!?

01:39:57.920 --> 01:39:58.550
Who is he?

01:39:59.260 --> 01:40:00.140
It's a secret.

01:40:05.310 --> 01:40:08.060
That dirty priest!

01:40:10.980 --> 01:40:14.860
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshioike.

01:40:15.610 --> 01:40:17.190
Yome-san Rokakku ...

01:40:17.400 --> 01:40:19.610
It's not "yome-san", it's "ane-san", idiot.

01:40:20.320 --> 01:40:22.160
Where did you learn that song?

01:40:22.820 --> 01:40:24.530
From my relatives in Kyoto.

01:40:25.540 --> 01:40:27.790
Was it sometime while I was in third grade?

01:40:28.250 --> 01:40:30.870
When I went to visit with you, I was taught it.

01:40:31.370 --> 01:40:31.960
With me?

01:40:32.250 --> 01:40:33.960
What? You don't remember?

01:40:34.460 --> 01:40:35.090
Oh yes,

01:40:35.630 --> 01:40:37.840
I remember you couldn't wait for my preparations,

01:40:38.170 --> 01:40:41.510
so you said you'd be going to Sannou Temple and left.

01:40:42.050 --> 01:40:42.720
That time,

01:40:43.010 --> 01:40:45.220
I was helped into wearing a kimono.

01:40:45.640 --> 01:40:46.850
I also did my hair,

01:40:47.100 --> 01:40:48.640
and wore a little bit of makeup.

01:40:49.270 --> 01:40:51.900
Then I went to go find you at Sannou Temple but,

01:40:52.270 --> 01:40:55.070
you weren't to be found anywhere, so I played with a ball.

01:40:56.480 --> 01:40:57.070
Really,

01:40:57.320 --> 01:40:58.990
I wish you could have seen it.

01:40:59.320 --> 01:41:02.450
The Sakura blossoms fluttered about, it was so beautiful!

01:41:03.240 --> 01:41:08.040
Marutake Ebisu Ni Oshioike.

01:41:08.700 --> 01:41:13.290
Yome-san Rokakku Takonishiki.

01:41:18.510 --> 01:41:20.380
So I was finally able to meet her.

01:41:21.760 --> 01:41:22.380
Meet her?

01:41:22.880 --> 01:41:24.800
You met your first love, Heiji?

01:41:25.300 --> 01:41:26.850
Who is it? Is it the dancing girl?

01:41:27.810 --> 01:41:30.180
Even if it takes a lifetime, I won't tell you, idiot.

01:41:30.680 --> 01:41:32.390
C'mon stingy, you can tell me.

01:41:32.640 --> 01:41:36.150
Alright, I'll tell you in another 1500 years.

01:41:37.070 --> 01:41:38.270
What does that mean!?

01:41:51.000 --> 01:41:51.910
Conan-kun!

01:41:52.040 --> 01:41:53.250
What are you doing?

01:41:58.290 --> 01:41:59.630
You're covered in sweat!

01:42:01.090 --> 01:42:03.090
Shi-Shinichi ...

01:42:04.470 --> 01:42:07.550
By the way, I gave Shinichi-niichan a call.

01:42:08.050 --> 01:42:12.390
I wanted him to appear as
Heiji-niichan and save Kazuha-neechan, right?

01:42:13.520 --> 01:42:14.100
Yes.

01:42:14.440 --> 01:42:17.110
But that guy was really weak.

01:42:18.150 --> 01:42:19.610
He escaped halfway.

01:42:20.440 --> 01:42:22.690
Even after you told me not to tell anyone else ...

01:42:26.570 --> 01:42:27.370
That's right ...

01:42:28.200 --> 01:42:31.240
So that really ... That really was Shinichi.

01:42:34.960 --> 01:42:36.080
I was finally able to meet you.

01:43:00.380 --> 01:43:04.650
moshimo, kimi ni meguri aetara

01:43:00.380 --> 01:43:04.650
If I had been able to meet you

01:43:05.200 --> 01:43:10.400
nidoto kimi no te wo hanasanai

01:43:05.200 --> 01:43:10.400
I wouldn't have let go of you ever again

01:43:10.650 --> 01:43:15.000
haru no owaritsugeru hanamidou

01:43:10.650 --> 01:43:15.000
The hanamidou tells of the end of spring

01:43:15.460 --> 01:43:20.370
kasumu hanahitohira

01:43:15.460 --> 01:43:20.370
One petal from this misty flower...

01:43:20.650 --> 01:43:25.780
yomigaeru omoide no uta

01:43:20.650 --> 01:43:25.780
And an old song floats back

01:43:25.800 --> 01:43:32.840
kono mune ni ima mo yasashiku

01:43:25.800 --> 01:43:32.840
Gently, even now, into my heart

01:43:33.120 --> 01:43:37.850
time after time kimi to deatta kiseki

01:43:33.120 --> 01:43:37.850
Time after time the miracle of meeting you

01:43:38.060 --> 01:43:43.260
yuruyaka na kaze fuku machi de

01:43:38.060 --> 01:43:43.260
In a city where the wind whispered through

01:43:43.550 --> 01:43:48.400
sotto te wo tsunagi aruita sakamichi

01:43:43.550 --> 01:43:48.400
We walked a path through the hills hand in hand

01:43:49.030 --> 01:43:57.530
ima mo wasurenai yakusoku

01:43:49.030 --> 01:43:57.530
And made an unforgettable promise

01:44:09.980 --> 01:44:14.510
kaze ni kimi no koe ga kikoeru

01:44:09.980 --> 01:44:14.510
I can hear your voice in the wind

01:44:14.850 --> 01:44:19.970
usurai saekaeru tooi kioku

01:44:14.850 --> 01:44:19.970
The thin ice freezes back over

01:44:20.250 --> 01:44:24.880
kizutsuku kowasa wo shirazu chikatta

01:44:20.250 --> 01:44:24.880
Long ago memories, not knowing to be afraid of hurt, I swore

01:44:25.190 --> 01:44:29.810
itsuka mata kono basho de

01:44:25.190 --> 01:44:29.810
That someday, we'd meet again

01:44:30.090 --> 01:44:35.360
meguriaou usubeni iro no

01:44:30.090 --> 01:44:35.360
Here, in a season of pale crimson

01:44:35.450 --> 01:44:42.490
kisetsu ga kuru hi ni egao de

01:44:35.450 --> 01:44:42.490
With smiles on our faces

01:44:42.770 --> 01:44:47.710
time after time hitori hana mau machi de

01:44:42.770 --> 01:44:47.710
Time after time Alone in the city of whirling blossoms

01:44:47.710 --> 01:44:52.960
chirazaru toki wa modoranai keredo

01:44:47.710 --> 01:44:52.960
Can't return to when things were fine

01:44:53.240 --> 01:44:58.150
ano hi to onaji kawaranai keshiki ni

01:44:53.240 --> 01:44:58.150
In this very same place, just like on that day

01:44:58.640 --> 01:45:07.100
namida hirari matte ita yo

01:44:58.640 --> 01:45:07.100
With my face strewn with tears, I waited for you

01:45:09.670 --> 01:45:19.660
kaze mau hanabira ga minamo wo naderu you ni

01:45:09.670 --> 01:45:19.660
Those petals fly in the whirling wind as if stroking the water's surface

01:45:19.660 --> 01:45:30.370
taisetsu ni omou hodo setsunaku

01:45:19.660 --> 01:45:30.370
In my anguish, I treasure each and every one...

01:45:32.610 --> 01:45:37.170
hito wa mina kodoku to iu keredo

01:45:32.610 --> 01:45:37.170
Everyone says that they're lonely

01:45:37.260 --> 01:45:42.570
sagasazu ni wa irarenai dareka wo

01:45:37.260 --> 01:45:42.570
That they have to keep searching for someone

01:45:42.870 --> 01:45:47.560
hakanaku koware yasui mono bakari

01:45:42.870 --> 01:45:47.560
But all they end up chasing after

01:45:47.770 --> 01:45:53.850
oimotomete shimau

01:45:47.770 --> 01:45:53.850
Are the fleeting and fragile

01:45:54.130 --> 01:45:59.850
Time after time kimi to irozuku machi de

01:45:54.130 --> 01:45:59.850
Time after time, If I could have met you in the city of changing hues

01:45:59.990 --> 01:46:05.200
Deaetara mou yakusoku wa iranai

01:45:59.990 --> 01:46:05.200
I wouldn't need any more promises

01:46:05.480 --> 01:46:10.700
Dare yorimo zutto kizutsuki yasui kimi no

01:46:05.480 --> 01:46:10.700
More than anyone else you are so easy to hurt

01:46:10.880 --> 01:46:19.410
Soba ni itai kondo wa kitto

01:46:10.880 --> 01:46:19.410
I want to be with you--this time, forever

01:46:55.470 --> 01:46:56.680
I'd like some ice cream.

01:46:56.970 --> 01:46:58.850
Note: 100 yen is roughly 1.00 USD

01:46:56.970 --> 01:46:58.850
Alright, it'll be 300 yen.

01:47:00.850 --> 01:47:04.270
In the end, I'm the only one who
couldn't meet the person I wanted to.

01:47:04.810 --> 01:47:07.940
Sonoko, you'll eventually be
able to meet Kyougoku-san for sure.

01:47:08.860 --> 01:47:09.860
But you know,

01:47:10.270 --> 01:47:13.570
I'm not that good at waiting for people.

01:47:14.400 --> 01:47:15.610
Isn't that true for you as well, Ran?

01:47:15.820 --> 01:47:16.280
Really?

01:47:17.070 --> 01:47:19.530
I don't mind waiting for people.

01:47:20.700 --> 01:47:23.370
Because the longer you wait,

01:47:23.830 --> 01:47:24.790
when you do meet ...

01:47:28.880 --> 01:47:31.170
You have the same expression as that time.

01:47:32.340 --> 01:47:33.420
you'll be more happy.

01:47:34.090 --> 01:47:35.050
Ah damn.

01:47:35.550 --> 01:47:38.970
If only Kudou-kun could have heard those words ...
